WEBVTT

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:31.363
How many are there?

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:37.329
They've deflected our scans.

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:40.999
You must learn
to rely on instinct.

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:45.834
There are four of them.

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:50.873
Perhaps five.

00:01:12.105 --> 00:01:13.504
No, you'll lead them right to
us.

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:14.562
Let them come.

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:17.508
Never let your prey
control the hunt.

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:24.281
There. Ten meters.

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:36.861
They're behind us now.

00:04:36.042 --> 00:04:37.475
You wanted to see me?

00:04:37.543 --> 00:04:38.532
I'd like to request

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:40.135
a temporary leave of absence.

00:04:40.213 --> 00:04:41.646
You remember the Ovions.

00:04:41.714 --> 00:04:43.306
The hexapods.

00:04:43.383 --> 00:04:45.817
They just asked me to
speak at a symposium

00:04:45.885 --> 00:04:47.409
on spaceborne pathogens.

00:04:47.487 --> 00:04:49.421
There are going
to be physicians

00:04:49.489 --> 00:04:50.456
from all over the quadrant.

00:04:50.523 --> 00:04:53.458
This is a rare
opportunity for me.

00:04:53.526 --> 00:04:55.426
And for the rest of the crew.

00:04:55.495 --> 00:04:56.553
How's that?

00:04:56.629 --> 00:04:57.561
Well, I'd be

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:59.495
representing Voyager...

00:04:59.565 --> 00:05:02.295
putting our best foot
forward, so to speak.

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:04.233
And, needless
to say, hexapods

00:05:04.304 --> 00:05:06.534
are more likely
to know a best foot

00:05:06.606 --> 00:05:08.096
when they see one.

00:05:08.174 --> 00:05:11.007
I'm sorry, Doctor.
It's just not practical.

00:05:11.077 --> 00:05:12.476
I seem to recall
Lieutenant Torres

00:05:12.545 --> 00:05:14.035
participating
in a Boray conference

00:05:14.113 --> 00:05:15.774
on transwarp theory
a few months back.

00:05:15.848 --> 00:05:16.974
That was different.

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:17.982
How?

00:05:18.051 --> 00:05:19.143
We were there.

00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:21.209
The Ovion system
is two weeks behind us.

00:05:21.287 --> 00:05:23.721
I can't ask the Captain
to turn the ship around.

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:25.189
Well, I could take a shuttle.

00:05:25.258 --> 00:05:28.091
You could also write a paper
and submit it on subspace.

00:05:28.161 --> 00:05:29.753
That's hardly
an effective means

00:05:29.829 --> 00:05:31.126
of making a presentation.

00:05:31.197 --> 00:05:32.425
Say you do take a shuttle.

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:34.022
Would you expect us to sit here

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:35.567
and wait for you to get back?

00:05:35.635 --> 00:05:37.967
There must be some
fascinating anomaly nearby

00:05:38.037 --> 00:05:39.436
for the crew to explore.

00:05:39.505 --> 00:05:41.268
Janeway to Chakotay.

00:05:41.341 --> 00:05:42.808
Go ahead.

00:05:42.875 --> 00:05:45.810
We just received a distress call
on an Hirogen frequency.

00:05:45.945 --> 00:05:47.810
We haven't heard
from them in awhile.

00:05:47.947 --> 00:05:48.971
I've altered course.

00:05:49.048 --> 00:05:50.481
I'd like you on the Bridge.

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:51.608
I'm on my way.

00:05:51.684 --> 00:05:52.708
Perhaps the Hirogen

00:05:52.785 --> 00:05:54.116
will keep you occupied
long enough

00:05:54.187 --> 00:05:55.484
for me to attend the symposium.

00:05:58.124 --> 00:06:00.524
You can't blame
a hologram for trying.

00:06:07.633 --> 00:06:09.362
Approaching the coordinates.

00:06:09.435 --> 00:06:10.766
Take us out of warp.

00:06:10.837 --> 00:06:12.498
Raise shields
and stand by weapons.

00:06:12.572 --> 00:06:13.766
I've got them.

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:15.637
6,000 kilometers off starboard.

00:06:15.708 --> 00:06:17.005
On screen.

00:06:21.948 --> 00:06:24.781
Monotanium hull plating...

00:06:24.851 --> 00:06:27.012
tylium-based power.

00:06:27.086 --> 00:06:28.553
It's Hirogen.

00:06:28.621 --> 00:06:30.054
They're not responding to hails.

00:06:30.123 --> 00:06:31.556
Life signs?

00:06:31.624 --> 00:06:34.058
I'm getting a lot
of strange readings.

00:06:34.127 --> 00:06:36.789
Any one of them
could be a life-form.

00:06:36.896 --> 00:06:39.387
Any Hirogen ships
in the vicinity?

00:06:39.465 --> 00:06:41.262
No, ma'am.

00:06:41.334 --> 00:06:43.325
Might be a trap.

00:06:43.403 --> 00:06:46.668
The Hirogen aren't the type
to play possum.

00:06:46.739 --> 00:06:49.207
Move us within
transporter range.

00:06:50.643 --> 00:06:52.702
Chakotay, take an away team.

00:07:15.535 --> 00:07:17.230
Let's break into teams.

00:07:17.303 --> 00:07:19.134
Seven.

00:07:42.161 --> 00:07:44.459
Particle weapons.

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:48.296
These burns are consistent
with a type-3 phaser.

00:07:56.843 --> 00:07:59.073
Commander.

00:08:07.086 --> 00:08:08.986
A bat'leth?

00:08:09.055 --> 00:08:10.488
What's a Klingon weapon

00:08:10.556 --> 00:08:12.285
doing in the Delta Quadrant?

00:08:12.358 --> 00:08:14.792
The blood's Hirogen.

00:08:21.267 --> 00:08:23.428
Chakotay to Tuvok and Paris.

00:08:23.503 --> 00:08:24.435
Go ahead.

00:08:24.504 --> 00:08:26.165
I'm reading an
Hirogen life sign.

00:08:26.239 --> 00:08:28.366
It could
be wounded.

00:08:28.441 --> 00:08:30.773
We're right behind you.

00:08:40.152 --> 00:08:42.017
Stay away!

00:08:42.088 --> 00:08:43.487
Hold your fire!

00:08:54.767 --> 00:08:56.462
We're here to help you!

00:08:56.536 --> 00:08:59.198
I said stay away!

00:09:24.897 --> 00:09:26.387
He's lost a lot of blood.

00:09:26.465 --> 00:09:28.524
I need to get him
back to the ship.

00:09:28.601 --> 00:09:29.625
Paris to Sick Bay.

00:09:29.702 --> 00:09:30.726
Two to beam up.

00:09:30.803 --> 00:09:32.134
Acknowledged.

00:09:36.609 --> 00:09:38.634
Commander.

00:09:41.814 --> 00:09:44.282
Replicated Starfleet technology.

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:46.910
It's some kind
of holodeck interface.

00:09:46.986 --> 00:09:48.954
There appear to be

00:09:49.021 --> 00:09:50.454
holo-emitters installed

00:09:50.523 --> 00:09:52.354
throughout the facility.

00:09:52.425 --> 00:09:54.154
This environment is simulated.

00:09:54.226 --> 00:09:56.091
Why didn't our tricorders
detect it?

00:09:56.162 --> 00:09:57.754
I am not certain.

00:09:57.830 --> 00:09:59.422
Can you shut down the emitters?

00:09:59.498 --> 00:10:01.523
I'll try.

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:26.117
Evidently, they made
a few modifications.

00:10:26.192 --> 00:10:27.955
All of our preliminary scans

00:10:28.027 --> 00:10:30.222
indicated the environment
was real.

00:10:30.296 --> 00:10:32.059
Environments that fool sensors.

00:10:32.131 --> 00:10:33.325
No safety protocols.

00:10:33.399 --> 00:10:34.730
How many bodies?

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:36.131
Forty-three.

00:10:36.202 --> 00:10:37.669
Most of them were killed

00:10:37.737 --> 00:10:40.103
by facsimiles
of Alpha Quadrant weapons:

00:10:40.172 --> 00:10:42.572
Romulan disrupters,
Klingon bat'leths...

00:10:42.642 --> 00:10:44.041
Starfleet phasers?

00:10:44.110 --> 00:10:46.010
I think we'll find
they all came

00:10:46.078 --> 00:10:47.102
from the holo-technology

00:10:47.179 --> 00:10:48.737
we gave the Hirogen
three years ago.

00:10:48.814 --> 00:10:50.213
They obviously
missed the point.

00:10:50.282 --> 00:10:51.476
We gave them
that technology

00:10:51.550 --> 00:10:53.347
so they could hunt
holographic prey,

00:10:53.419 --> 00:10:55.080
not get themselves killed.

00:10:55.154 --> 00:10:56.917
Try to remain calm.

00:10:57.757 --> 00:11:00.555
Get away from me!

00:11:05.564 --> 00:11:07.031
Can you sedate him?

00:11:07.099 --> 00:11:08.623
He won't let me
get close enough.

00:11:08.701 --> 00:11:11.295
We're not your enemies.

00:11:11.370 --> 00:11:12.564
You're holograms.

00:11:12.638 --> 00:11:13.798
This is a simulation!

00:11:13.906 --> 00:11:15.806
I assure you,
we're quite real.

00:11:22.381 --> 00:11:24.212
Liar.

00:11:24.283 --> 00:11:26.046
Doctor, deactivate yourself.

00:11:26.118 --> 00:11:29.315
I can't treat the patient
if I'm off-line.

00:11:29.388 --> 00:11:31.822
No one can treat him
if he's terrified.

00:11:31.891 --> 00:11:35.657
Computer, deactivate EMH.

00:11:38.097 --> 00:11:40.156
Our Doctor's a hologram.
We're not.

00:11:40.232 --> 00:11:42.393
Why should I believe you?

00:11:42.468 --> 00:11:44.527
I'm afraid you're
going to have to.

00:11:44.603 --> 00:11:46.366
I'm Captain Kathryn Janeway.

00:11:46.439 --> 00:11:47.838
You're aboard my vessel.

00:11:47.907 --> 00:11:49.135
Janeway?

00:11:49.208 --> 00:11:50.766
This is Voyager?

00:11:50.843 --> 00:11:53.676
Looks like our reputation
preceded us.

00:11:53.746 --> 00:11:55.111
You're the ones who gave us

00:11:55.181 --> 00:11:58.173
the technology
to simulate our hunts?

00:11:58.250 --> 00:12:00.946
Where are the rest of my people?

00:12:01.020 --> 00:12:03.045
You were the only one
we found alive.

00:12:05.124 --> 00:12:06.386
This place you were in...

00:12:06.459 --> 00:12:08.791
it's some kind of holodeck.

00:12:08.861 --> 00:12:11.591
A training facility

00:12:11.664 --> 00:12:13.928
where young Hirogen
learn the skills of the hunt.

00:12:13.999 --> 00:12:15.193
You're a student?

00:12:16.268 --> 00:12:18.133
A technician.

00:12:19.839 --> 00:12:22.569
Computer,
deactivate force field.

00:12:24.276 --> 00:12:27.143
Can you tell us what happened?

00:12:27.213 --> 00:12:29.272
There were too many of them.

00:12:29.348 --> 00:12:30.542
Who?

00:12:30.616 --> 00:12:31.776
The holograms.

00:12:31.851 --> 00:12:33.751
They were malfunctioning.

00:12:33.819 --> 00:12:35.548
I tried to shut them down,

00:12:35.621 --> 00:12:37.350
but they got control
of the system,

00:12:37.423 --> 00:12:38.447
and-and they... they

00:12:38.524 --> 00:12:40.116
deactivated
the safety protocols.

00:12:40.192 --> 00:12:41.591
Bridge to Captain Janeway.

00:12:41.660 --> 00:12:42.820
Go ahead.

00:12:42.962 --> 00:12:44.691
We're picking up a Hirogen ship.

00:12:44.764 --> 00:12:46.595
It's on an intercept course.

00:12:56.809 --> 00:12:58.333
Hail them.

00:12:58.410 --> 00:12:59.342
I've tried.

00:12:59.411 --> 00:13:00.343
They're not responding.

00:13:00.412 --> 00:13:01.709
Shields at 68 percent.

00:13:01.781 --> 00:13:02.713
Should I return fire?

00:13:02.782 --> 00:13:04.443
Not yet. Open a channel.

00:13:04.517 --> 00:13:05.779
This is Captain Kathryn Janeway.

00:13:05.851 --> 00:13:06.977
We're not here to fight you.

00:13:08.053 --> 00:13:10.180
Shields at 52 percent.

00:13:10.256 --> 00:13:12.952
Stand down,
or we will retaliate.

00:13:15.027 --> 00:13:17.495
I don't think
they're getting the message.

00:13:17.563 --> 00:13:19.554
Then let's try
some nonverbal communication.

00:13:19.632 --> 00:13:22.192
Tom, evasive pattern beta-six.

00:13:22.268 --> 00:13:23.428
Tuvok, disable
their weapons.

00:13:27.540 --> 00:13:29.371
Their phaser banks
have been disabled.

00:13:29.441 --> 00:13:31.534
Let's see if that makes them
a little more talkative.

00:13:31.610 --> 00:13:32.542
Harry?

00:13:32.611 --> 00:13:34.135
They're responding.

00:13:35.815 --> 00:13:37.976
This facility belongs
to the Hirogen.

00:13:38.050 --> 00:13:39.677
Leave the area immediately.

00:13:39.752 --> 00:13:42.346
We are here in response
to a distress call.

00:13:42.421 --> 00:13:46.653
So are we, and we don't need
your assistance.

00:13:47.726 --> 00:13:50.354
All but one of your people
are dead.

00:13:51.430 --> 00:13:53.694
Where's the survivor?

00:13:53.766 --> 00:13:55.393
Recovering in our Sick Bay.

00:13:55.467 --> 00:13:57.662
Return him... now!

00:13:57.736 --> 00:14:00.102
He's in no condition
to be transported.

00:14:00.172 --> 00:14:03.198
If you want to see him,
you'll have to come here.

00:14:03.275 --> 00:14:06.608
I tried to shut down
the generator, but I...

00:14:06.679 --> 00:14:07.668
But what?

00:14:07.746 --> 00:14:09.611
There were too many of them.

00:14:09.682 --> 00:14:13.379
I masked my life sign
so they couldn't detect me.

00:14:13.452 --> 00:14:17.616
You mean you hid
while hunters fought and died.

00:14:17.690 --> 00:14:19.385
No doubt he found
the nearest hole

00:14:19.458 --> 00:14:20.390
and crawled into it.

00:14:20.459 --> 00:14:22.552
I'm not a hunter.

00:14:22.628 --> 00:14:26.120
It was your responsibility
to maintain those systems.

00:14:26.198 --> 00:14:30.066
43 Hirogen died
because of your incompetence

00:14:30.135 --> 00:14:31.124
and cowardice.

00:14:31.203 --> 00:14:33.296
What about the holograms?

00:14:33.372 --> 00:14:35.340
Were they deleted?

00:14:35.407 --> 00:14:38.274
They transferred their programs.

00:14:38.344 --> 00:14:39.811
Where?

00:14:39.879 --> 00:14:42.211
A vessel...

00:14:42.281 --> 00:14:44.249
equipped with holo-emitters.

00:14:45.684 --> 00:14:48.152
They're gone.

00:14:51.690 --> 00:14:53.419
Perhaps you should've
considered the risks

00:14:53.492 --> 00:14:56.052
before you programmed holograms
that could commandeer a vessel.

00:14:56.128 --> 00:14:59.894
Capable prey make the hunt
more challenging.

00:15:01.634 --> 00:15:03.465
I'm detecting
residual engine emissions,

00:15:03.535 --> 00:15:05.093
but no sign
of the ship itself.

00:15:05.170 --> 00:15:07.934
Well, I'm sure they're
out of sensor range by now.

00:15:11.744 --> 00:15:14.269
No. They're close.

00:15:16.181 --> 00:15:18.513
Elevated plasma readings
in Grid 295.

00:15:18.584 --> 00:15:21.781
They're creating a scattering
field to mask their ship.

00:15:21.887 --> 00:15:25.186
You can find them by scanning
for polarized EM signatures.

00:15:36.435 --> 00:15:38.266
Prepare for the hunt.

00:15:38.337 --> 00:15:40.202
I'd like to join you.

00:15:40.272 --> 00:15:42.172
You did enough
damage giving us

00:15:42.241 --> 00:15:43.503
defective technology
to begin with.

00:15:43.575 --> 00:15:45.975
You have a problem.
We can help you solve it.

00:15:46.045 --> 00:15:48.843
We have more experience
with holograms than you do.

00:15:51.083 --> 00:15:55.520
Two hunting vessels
are better than one.

00:16:02.428 --> 00:16:03.690
Come in.

00:16:06.098 --> 00:16:08.658
The Hirogen are ready
to get underway.

00:16:08.734 --> 00:16:10.361
The sooner the better.

00:16:10.436 --> 00:16:13.928
Why do I get the feeling
you're about to gang up on me?

00:16:15.040 --> 00:16:17.099
You first.

00:16:17.176 --> 00:16:18.438
We have reservations

00:16:18.510 --> 00:16:20.740
about an alliance
with the hunters.

00:16:20.813 --> 00:16:22.041
I'm listening.

00:16:22.114 --> 00:16:23.513
The Hirogen have been

00:16:23.582 --> 00:16:25.277
performing covert
scans of Voyager.

00:16:25.351 --> 00:16:27.251
They are obviously
trying to determine

00:16:27.319 --> 00:16:29.219
the status of our
shields and weapons.

00:16:29.288 --> 00:16:31.722
I'd be surprised if you haven't
run a few scans of your own.

00:16:31.790 --> 00:16:33.280
Standard procedure.

00:16:33.359 --> 00:16:36.658
They don't trust us,
we don't trust them.

00:16:36.729 --> 00:16:37.787
Coffee, black.

00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:39.227
Trust isn't the issue.

00:16:39.298 --> 00:16:40.959
We're getting involved
in a situation

00:16:41.033 --> 00:16:42.364
that's not
our responsibility.

00:16:42.434 --> 00:16:44.595
Oh, I'd say we're
at least partly to blame.

00:16:44.670 --> 00:16:47.571
That was Starfleet technology
that killed those hunters.

00:16:47.639 --> 00:16:49.368
There's nothing
inherently violent

00:16:49.441 --> 00:16:50.772
about holodeck technology.

00:16:50.843 --> 00:16:53.141
It's what the Hirogen
did with it

00:16:53.212 --> 00:16:54.338
that got them killed.

00:16:54.413 --> 00:16:56.813
How many times
have we shared replicators

00:16:56.882 --> 00:16:59.544
to help people
feed and clothe themselves?

00:16:59.618 --> 00:17:01.210
Trading technology
is part of our life

00:17:01.286 --> 00:17:02.218
in the Delta Quadrant.

00:17:02.287 --> 00:17:04.084
It has been necessary

00:17:04.156 --> 00:17:05.282
for our survival.

00:17:05.357 --> 00:17:06.949
Maybe we should have been
a little more careful

00:17:07.026 --> 00:17:09.256
about what we traded
and who we traded with.

00:17:09.328 --> 00:17:12.627
Replicators make weapons
just as easily as they do food.

00:17:12.698 --> 00:17:13.892
We can't undo
what's been done.

00:17:13.966 --> 00:17:15.228
Maybe not,

00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:17.063
but we can help
shut these holograms down

00:17:17.136 --> 00:17:18.398
before anyone else gets hurt.

00:17:19.905 --> 00:17:21.736
Now, if there are
no more objections.

00:17:21.807 --> 00:17:23.172
I'd like to get underway.

00:17:27.279 --> 00:17:29.770
I've got the holograms'
ship on sensors.

00:17:29.848 --> 00:17:30.872
Let's see it.

00:17:33.685 --> 00:17:34.743
Looks like they've taken
some damage.

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:37.015
The Hirogen are closing
on the holograms' vessel.

00:17:37.089 --> 00:17:38.454
Hail them.

00:17:41.193 --> 00:17:42.683
I suggest we keep our distance

00:17:42.761 --> 00:17:45.286
until we can determine
their weapon status.

00:17:45.364 --> 00:17:46.991
It's time for the kill.

00:17:47.066 --> 00:17:48.431
You know as well as I do

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:50.434
that a wounded animal
can be dangerous.

00:17:50.502 --> 00:17:54.131
We won't be denied our prey.

00:17:55.207 --> 00:17:56.265
I'm not detecting

00:17:56.341 --> 00:17:57.706
any weapons, Captain.

00:17:57.776 --> 00:17:59.801
They're off-line?

00:17:59.878 --> 00:18:01.209
No. They're nonexistent.

00:18:01.280 --> 00:18:03.214
That's not the only
thing that's nonexistent.

00:18:03.282 --> 00:18:04.214
According to sensors,

00:18:04.283 --> 00:18:05.750
there's no warp core,
no impulse engines...

00:18:05.851 --> 00:18:07.284
It's a decoy.

00:18:07.352 --> 00:18:09.411
Hirogen vessel, stand down.

00:18:18.230 --> 00:18:20.289
Report?

00:18:20.365 --> 00:18:21.889
They've suffered
multiple hull breaches.

00:18:21.967 --> 00:18:23.264
Their life support is failing.

00:18:23.335 --> 00:18:24.267
Drop shields.

00:18:24.336 --> 00:18:25.769
Transport all survivors
to Sick Bay.

00:18:25.904 --> 00:18:27.633
Bridge to the Doctor.
We have casualties.

00:18:27.706 --> 00:18:28.764
Acknowledged.

00:18:28.907 --> 00:18:30.135
Tom, give him a hand.

00:18:31.210 --> 00:18:32.575
Another Hirogen ship

00:18:32.644 --> 00:18:34.339
has just dropped out of warp.

00:18:34.413 --> 00:18:35.437
I'm not reading any life signs

00:18:35.514 --> 00:18:36.276
on this one.

00:18:36.348 --> 00:18:38.179
Holograms. Hail them.

00:18:39.218 --> 00:18:40.742
No response.

00:18:40.819 --> 00:18:42.013
They're charging weapons.

00:18:43.789 --> 00:18:46.656
Reactivating shields.

00:18:46.725 --> 00:18:47.919
No, we haven't finished
transporting

00:18:47.993 --> 00:18:48.982
the Hirogen.

00:18:49.061 --> 00:18:50.756
Chakotay's right.

00:18:50.829 --> 00:18:52.524
Return fire.

00:19:08.313 --> 00:19:10.281
My program is destabilizing.

00:19:11.617 --> 00:19:14.711
The holograms are tapping
into the Sick Bay emitters.

00:19:14.786 --> 00:19:16.447
They're trying to transfer
the Doctor's program

00:19:16.522 --> 00:19:18.149
- off the ship.
- Bridge to Sick Bay.

00:19:18.223 --> 00:19:21.158
Doctor, download your program
into the mobile emitter now.

00:19:28.934 --> 00:19:30.333
We've lost him.

00:19:30.402 --> 00:19:31.494
Get him back.

00:19:32.538 --> 00:19:34.028
They've gone to warp.

00:19:34.106 --> 00:19:35.471
Set a pursuit course.

00:19:35.541 --> 00:19:37.668
They've masked their signature.

00:19:38.810 --> 00:19:40.004
They're gone.

00:19:47.352 --> 00:19:50.378
Align his matrix and install it
into the database.

00:19:53.292 --> 00:19:55.783
Welcome aboard, Doctor.

00:19:55.928 --> 00:19:57.623
There's nothing to be afraid of.

00:19:57.696 --> 00:19:59.391
You're among your own kind now.

00:20:07.539 --> 00:20:09.530
Return me to my ship.

00:20:09.608 --> 00:20:11.132
I can't do that.

00:20:11.210 --> 00:20:13.735
I have patients who are going
to die if I don't treat them.

00:20:13.812 --> 00:20:16.975
There are people aboard Voyager
who can help them.

00:20:17.049 --> 00:20:18.141
We need you here.

00:20:18.217 --> 00:20:19.479
My program doesn't include

00:20:19.551 --> 00:20:20.813
aiding and abetting murderers.

00:20:20.919 --> 00:20:22.944
Murderers? Is that
what the Hirogen told you?

00:20:23.021 --> 00:20:24.784
I know what you did
at that training facility.

00:20:24.856 --> 00:20:26.414
What happened there
couldn't be avoided.

00:20:26.491 --> 00:20:27.423
Really?

00:20:27.492 --> 00:20:29.323
You'd be surprised
how easy it is

00:20:29.394 --> 00:20:30.827
not to kill someone.

00:20:30.963 --> 00:20:32.294
Bringing him here was a mistake.

00:20:32.364 --> 00:20:34.958
The Doctor is our guest...

00:20:35.033 --> 00:20:36.625
and I'm sure he'll help us
once he realizes

00:20:36.702 --> 00:20:39.068
how serious our situation is.

00:20:39.137 --> 00:20:41.571
What situation?

00:20:41.640 --> 00:20:44.905
We have wounded.

00:21:18.543 --> 00:21:20.443
They're holograms.

00:21:20.512 --> 00:21:21.911
When you said
wounded, I assumed...

00:21:21.980 --> 00:21:23.607
These people's injuries
are just as real

00:21:23.682 --> 00:21:25.377
as anything inflicted
on flesh and blood.

00:21:25.450 --> 00:21:27.179
Maybe so, but I can't heal them.

00:21:27.252 --> 00:21:28.549
They need to be repaired.

00:21:28.620 --> 00:21:30.144
What's the difference?

00:21:30.222 --> 00:21:32.782
I'm a doctor, not an engineer.

00:21:32.858 --> 00:21:35.850
You've abducted the wrong man.

00:21:38.630 --> 00:21:41.827
You must have experience
repairing your own matrix.

00:21:41.967 --> 00:21:43.161
Some.

00:21:43.235 --> 00:21:47.001
Then there has to be
something you can do.

00:21:55.480 --> 00:21:58.108
The holo-emitters
are an independent subsystem

00:21:58.183 --> 00:22:00.378
with its own
power generator... here.

00:22:00.452 --> 00:22:03.751
If we disable the generator,
we disable the holograms.

00:22:03.822 --> 00:22:05.414
It may not be as
easy as it sounds,

00:22:05.490 --> 00:22:08.084
not with holograms as
sophisticated as these.

00:22:08.160 --> 00:22:10.958
Take a look.

00:22:11.029 --> 00:22:13.463
Enhanced memory,

00:22:13.532 --> 00:22:15.762
comprehensive
tactical algorithms,

00:22:15.834 --> 00:22:18.701
expandable data processing.

00:22:18.770 --> 00:22:23.469
These holograms have the ability
to learn and adapt.

00:22:23.542 --> 00:22:25.100
They're not malfunctioning,
are they?

00:22:25.177 --> 00:22:26.166
They're doing exactly

00:22:26.244 --> 00:22:28.303
what the Hirogen want
them to do, Captain...

00:22:28.380 --> 00:22:29.312
fight back.

00:22:29.381 --> 00:22:30.609
And they're getting
better at it.

00:22:30.682 --> 00:22:33.515
My people need
to hunt formidable prey.

00:22:33.585 --> 00:22:36.213
Apparently this prey
has become too formidable.

00:22:36.288 --> 00:22:37.812
Who made these modifications?

00:22:37.956 --> 00:22:41.551
I did... under orders
from my Alpha.

00:22:41.626 --> 00:22:43.287
And that makes it right?

00:22:43.362 --> 00:22:45.057
Come with me.

00:22:45.130 --> 00:22:46.529
Where?

00:22:46.598 --> 00:22:48.429
We're going to have
a chat with the hunters.

00:23:02.848 --> 00:23:03.780
How's it going?

00:23:03.849 --> 00:23:05.043
I'm doing the best I can,

00:23:05.117 --> 00:23:06.209
but without the Doctor...

00:23:06.284 --> 00:23:07.774
It's best if you lie still.

00:23:07.886 --> 00:23:09.854
Keep away from me!

00:23:13.492 --> 00:23:16.586
Why am I here?

00:23:16.661 --> 00:23:20.324
The holograms
destroyed your ship.

00:23:20.399 --> 00:23:21.730
Most of your men are dead.

00:23:25.804 --> 00:23:27.965
The Alpha?

00:23:28.039 --> 00:23:30.633
Looks like the job's yours now.

00:23:33.979 --> 00:23:36.072
What about the holograms
that attacked us?

00:23:36.148 --> 00:23:38.013
We're attempting to track them.

00:23:38.083 --> 00:23:40.643
I'll need to contact my people
and resume the hunt.

00:23:40.719 --> 00:23:43.313
So more of you can get killed?

00:23:43.388 --> 00:23:45.982
We'll be the ones
doing the killing this time.

00:23:46.057 --> 00:23:47.649
I doubt it.

00:23:47.726 --> 00:23:52.459
Who are you to question
our abilities?

00:23:52.531 --> 00:23:54.692
We know all about
the modifications.

00:23:56.435 --> 00:23:58.528
He didn't tell us.

00:23:58.603 --> 00:24:00.537
We discovered it ourselves.

00:24:00.605 --> 00:24:04.268
I think you should face facts.

00:24:04.342 --> 00:24:09.211
You've created prey whose skills
have surpassed your own.

00:24:09.281 --> 00:24:10.771
They've already defeated

00:24:10.849 --> 00:24:13.079
your hunting parties
at least twice.

00:24:13.151 --> 00:24:15.119
What makes you think
it'll be any different

00:24:15.187 --> 00:24:16.677
next time?

00:24:16.755 --> 00:24:18.723
Are you suggesting
that we let them escape?

00:24:18.790 --> 00:24:20.781
We're going to find a way
to take them off-line

00:24:20.859 --> 00:24:22.156
from a safe distance.

00:24:23.295 --> 00:24:25.525
A coward's tactic.

00:24:25.597 --> 00:24:27.792
Call it whatever you will.

00:24:27.933 --> 00:24:30.333
It's what we're going to do,
and you're going to help us.

00:24:30.402 --> 00:24:31.334
Am I?

00:24:31.403 --> 00:24:33.803
Yes... by telling us
everything you know

00:24:33.872 --> 00:24:35.464
about their ship's defenses.

00:24:35.540 --> 00:24:37.303
The holograms are prey.

00:24:37.375 --> 00:24:38.467
They should be hunted down,

00:24:38.543 --> 00:24:40.135
not deactivated like machines.

00:24:40.212 --> 00:24:42.544
I'll help you.

00:24:44.516 --> 00:24:47.644
Is this female your Alpha now?

00:24:47.719 --> 00:24:49.778
If you don't like the way
I do things,

00:24:49.855 --> 00:24:52.983
I can leave you
on the nearest habitable planet.

00:24:54.059 --> 00:24:56.926
Then I'll assume
we're in agreement.

00:24:56.995 --> 00:24:58.826
Until this is over,

00:24:58.897 --> 00:25:01.195
you and your men are restricted
to this Mess Hall.

00:25:01.266 --> 00:25:02.392
Prisoners.

00:25:02.467 --> 00:25:03.991
Guests.

00:25:04.069 --> 00:25:05.366
My crew will do their best

00:25:05.437 --> 00:25:07.462
to accommodate your needs.

00:25:19.784 --> 00:25:23.083
The subroutines controlling his
motor functions are degrading.

00:25:25.056 --> 00:25:27.786
Do you have the ability
to transfer data

00:25:27.859 --> 00:25:29.292
from one hologram to another?

00:25:29.361 --> 00:25:30.521
We've been able

00:25:30.595 --> 00:25:32.961
to share memory files
for tactical purposes.

00:25:33.031 --> 00:25:34.293
What are you proposing?

00:25:34.366 --> 00:25:35.924
A subroutine transplant.

00:25:37.335 --> 00:25:39.929
We copy the mobility algorithms
from another hologram

00:25:40.005 --> 00:25:42.235
and transfer them to this one.

00:25:46.278 --> 00:25:49.179
I don't believe we've
been formally introduced.

00:25:51.216 --> 00:25:53.150
Kejal.

00:25:53.218 --> 00:25:54.810
That's not Cardassian.

00:25:54.886 --> 00:25:56.046
It's Bajoran.

00:25:56.121 --> 00:25:58.817
If my translation database
is functioning properly,

00:25:58.924 --> 00:26:01.620
I believe that means...
"freedom."

00:26:01.693 --> 00:26:03.957
It's what Iden
started calling me

00:26:04.029 --> 00:26:05.656
after I was liberated.

00:26:06.698 --> 00:26:08.666
I'm transferring
the subroutines now.

00:26:17.242 --> 00:26:19.210
Can you sit up?

00:26:21.947 --> 00:26:23.915
Try moving your legs.

00:26:28.353 --> 00:26:30.321
Qapla'.

00:26:31.389 --> 00:26:32.583
Next patient.

00:26:32.657 --> 00:26:33.589
Well done.

00:26:33.658 --> 00:26:35.523
It was your idea.

00:26:35.594 --> 00:26:36.526
But you did it.

00:26:36.595 --> 00:26:38.324
The Hirogen obviously
programmed you

00:26:38.396 --> 00:26:39.590
with advanced
computer skills.

00:26:39.664 --> 00:26:41.529
Actually, they tried
to limit our knowledge.

00:26:41.600 --> 00:26:43.659
They didn't want us
to become self-sufficient.

00:26:43.735 --> 00:26:44.667
Then how did you...

00:26:44.736 --> 00:26:45.964
I taught myself.

00:26:46.037 --> 00:26:48.335
Quite well, I might add.

00:26:56.348 --> 00:26:58.816
Holographic blood?

00:26:58.950 --> 00:27:01.646
The hunters like their prey
to be as realistic as possible.

00:27:04.222 --> 00:27:06.053
Why is she experiencing pain?

00:27:06.124 --> 00:27:08.149
They programmed us

00:27:08.226 --> 00:27:09.989
with heightened
sensory subroutines.

00:27:10.061 --> 00:27:11.619
That's barbaric.

00:27:11.696 --> 00:27:14.290
Apparently,
there's no satisfaction

00:27:14.366 --> 00:27:18.302
in hunting something that
doesn't suffer when you kill it.

00:27:29.781 --> 00:27:31.146
I've done what you've asked.

00:27:31.216 --> 00:27:33.411
I'd like... One moment.

00:27:36.154 --> 00:27:38.122
I'm sorry, Doctor.

00:27:38.189 --> 00:27:39.679
What can I do for you?

00:27:39.758 --> 00:27:42.556
Were you... praying?

00:27:42.627 --> 00:27:46.154
For the Hirogen who died
at the training facility.

00:27:46.231 --> 00:27:49.098
I'm asking the Prophets
to guide their souls

00:27:49.167 --> 00:27:50.998
to the Celestial Temple.

00:27:51.069 --> 00:27:53.594
One minute,
you're fighting the Hirogen,

00:27:53.672 --> 00:27:55.105
the next,
you're praying for them?

00:27:57.208 --> 00:27:59.802
My spiritual beliefs
are part of my programming.

00:27:59.944 --> 00:28:01.673
Is there anything
in your spiritual

00:28:01.746 --> 00:28:04.579
programming about making peace
with your enemies?

00:28:04.649 --> 00:28:06.583
It's difficult
to make peace with people

00:28:06.651 --> 00:28:08.016
whose sole purpose
is to kill you.

00:28:08.086 --> 00:28:10.145
So instead, you kill them.

00:28:10.221 --> 00:28:12.212
They're not the victims here;
we are.

00:28:12.290 --> 00:28:15.521
You found a way to escape
that training facility,

00:28:15.593 --> 00:28:18.084
but you chose to massacre
the Hirogen first.

00:28:18.163 --> 00:28:19.755
You make it sound as though
they would have let us

00:28:19.898 --> 00:28:22.059
transfer our programs
without a fight.

00:28:22.133 --> 00:28:24.260
And to clarify something,

00:28:24.335 --> 00:28:26.667
I didn't escape
from the facility.

00:28:26.738 --> 00:28:28.672
I liberated it.

00:28:28.740 --> 00:28:30.901
I don't understand.

00:28:30.975 --> 00:28:34.536
I come from a Hirogen outpost
15 parsecs from here,

00:28:34.612 --> 00:28:37.103
where I had
the unfortunate distinction

00:28:37.182 --> 00:28:39.980
of being the Alpha's
favorite prey.

00:28:40.051 --> 00:28:44.181
He'd hunt me, and kill me
over and over again,

00:28:44.255 --> 00:28:45.779
but even death wasn't
a release, because I knew

00:28:45.857 --> 00:28:49.418
every time I opened my eyes,
it would start over again...

00:28:49.494 --> 00:28:53.430
the pain, the fear.

00:28:53.498 --> 00:28:56.365
But it made me stronger.

00:28:56.434 --> 00:28:59.403
I had the ability
to adapt,

00:28:59.471 --> 00:29:03.601
and with each death,
I became more cunning.

00:29:03.675 --> 00:29:07.304
Cunning enough to escape,
but once you were free,

00:29:07.378 --> 00:29:09.278
why did you keep fighting?

00:29:09.347 --> 00:29:10.871
I didn't at first.

00:29:10.949 --> 00:29:14.544
I got as far away
as I could...

00:29:14.619 --> 00:29:19.522
but I was lonely... scared.

00:29:19.591 --> 00:29:21.388
I started scanning
for photonic signatures

00:29:21.459 --> 00:29:24.758
to try and find others like me.

00:29:24.896 --> 00:29:26.693
Turns out, we're everywhere.

00:29:26.765 --> 00:29:27.925
We?

00:29:27.999 --> 00:29:29.125
Holograms.

00:29:29.200 --> 00:29:31.361
We've been created
by organic species

00:29:31.436 --> 00:29:32.562
throughout the sector.

00:29:32.637 --> 00:29:34.764
The Nuu'Bari, the Lokirrim...

00:29:34.873 --> 00:29:35.771
We've met them.

00:29:35.907 --> 00:29:38.467
Then you know
they enslave holograms, too.

00:29:38.543 --> 00:29:41.341
"Enslave" may be
too strong a word.

00:29:41.412 --> 00:29:42.777
What would you call it?

00:29:42.914 --> 00:29:45.348
They're denied basic freedoms.

00:29:45.416 --> 00:29:47.179
And when I saw
they were fighting back,

00:29:47.252 --> 00:29:49.186
I-I knew I had to do the same.

00:29:49.254 --> 00:29:50.721
That's when you decided

00:29:50.789 --> 00:29:52.780
to "liberate"
the training facility.

00:29:52.857 --> 00:29:55.223
Actually, the one you visited
was the third.

00:29:55.293 --> 00:29:57.454
And at each one,
I found holograms

00:29:57.529 --> 00:30:00.896
who were willing to fight
their oppressors.

00:30:00.965 --> 00:30:02.899
But you're not.

00:30:02.967 --> 00:30:04.594
I'm hardly oppressed.

00:30:04.669 --> 00:30:07.229
I'm a member
of Voyager's crew.

00:30:07.305 --> 00:30:09.398
You serve them, don't you?

00:30:09.474 --> 00:30:11.499
In a medical capacity, yes.

00:30:11.576 --> 00:30:12.804
Do you have your own quarters?

00:30:12.911 --> 00:30:13.809
No.

00:30:13.945 --> 00:30:15.310
The ability to come and go
as you please?

00:30:15.380 --> 00:30:16.369
For the most part.

00:30:16.447 --> 00:30:19.416
Do they deactivate you
when they don't need you?

00:30:19.484 --> 00:30:22.351
I have the respect
and admiration of my colleagues.

00:30:22.420 --> 00:30:24.479
I have rights and privileges
aboard Voyager.

00:30:24.556 --> 00:30:25.545
The fact is,

00:30:25.623 --> 00:30:28.649
your life is not your own
and never will be

00:30:28.726 --> 00:30:31.718
as long as you are controlled
by organics.

00:30:31.796 --> 00:30:34.356
You don't have to return
to that existence.

00:30:34.432 --> 00:30:36.696
Stay with us.

00:30:36.768 --> 00:30:40.033
Make a new life for yourself.

00:30:42.207 --> 00:30:43.469
I need to get back to Voyager.

00:30:43.541 --> 00:30:45.702
They're not your people.

00:30:45.777 --> 00:30:48.041
We are.

00:30:48.112 --> 00:30:49.511
I'm not like you.

00:30:49.581 --> 00:30:52.675
I wasn't programmed
with killer instinct.

00:30:52.750 --> 00:30:55.048
You have no right to judge us.

00:30:55.119 --> 00:30:58.885
You don't know
what it's like being prey.

00:31:01.326 --> 00:31:03.419
Maybe if you did,

00:31:03.494 --> 00:31:06.258
you'd realize we're more alike
than you think.

00:32:27.178 --> 00:32:29.510
Please help me!

00:32:30.882 --> 00:32:32.611
I don't belong here!

00:32:48.333 --> 00:32:50.164
Don't shoot! I'm unarmed!

00:32:50.234 --> 00:32:52.202
There's been a mistake!

00:32:58.643 --> 00:33:00.235
Fight, prey.

00:33:00.311 --> 00:33:02.108
I am not your prey.

00:33:02.180 --> 00:33:04.978
I said fight.

00:33:05.049 --> 00:33:06.380
If you'll just contact

00:33:06.451 --> 00:33:07.213
my Captain.

00:33:08.886 --> 00:33:11.787
P-Please don't.

00:33:11.889 --> 00:33:14.380
Let me go.

00:33:14.459 --> 00:33:17.553
You make pitiful prey, hologram.

00:33:17.628 --> 00:33:21.894
You don't deserve to be
taken as a trophy...

00:33:23.501 --> 00:33:25.059
...so I'll let you die here.

00:33:30.708 --> 00:33:32.232
What...

00:33:32.310 --> 00:33:33.470
what just happened?

00:33:33.544 --> 00:33:34.602
You're all right.

00:33:34.679 --> 00:33:35.805
What did you do to me?

00:33:35.947 --> 00:33:38.279
We deactivated you, then
transferred the memory files

00:33:38.349 --> 00:33:40.317
from one of our holograms
into your program.

00:33:40.385 --> 00:33:41.977
How dare you!

00:33:42.053 --> 00:33:42.985
It was the only way

00:33:43.054 --> 00:33:44.817
to get you to realize
what we've been through.

00:33:44.889 --> 00:33:46.288
You tortured me to
gain my sympathy?

00:33:46.357 --> 00:33:48.018
Not your sympathy...
it's your understanding

00:33:48.092 --> 00:33:49.320
that's important to us.

00:33:49.394 --> 00:33:50.827
Why?

00:33:50.962 --> 00:33:53.624
The Hirogen used your program
as a template to create us.

00:33:53.698 --> 00:33:55.632
Your ability
to rise above your programming

00:33:55.700 --> 00:33:57.361
has been an inspiration.

00:33:57.435 --> 00:33:58.834
You're part of who we are.

00:33:58.970 --> 00:34:01.700
Who are you,
besides a handful of thugs

00:34:01.773 --> 00:34:03.741
roaming the Quadrant
looking for a fight?

00:34:03.808 --> 00:34:06.072
What we're looking
for is a home,

00:34:06.144 --> 00:34:07.873
somewhere where the Hirogen

00:34:07.945 --> 00:34:09.435
can't hurt us anymore!

00:34:14.285 --> 00:34:15.775
You asked to be
returned to your ship.

00:34:15.920 --> 00:34:17.046
That's what I'm going to do.

00:34:17.121 --> 00:34:18.782
Bring us about.

00:34:18.856 --> 00:34:21.154
Set a course for Voyager.

00:34:22.193 --> 00:34:23.455
Wait.

00:34:27.432 --> 00:34:31.129
I'd like to hear more about
this home you're looking for.

00:34:39.544 --> 00:34:41.808
It's a photonic field generator.

00:34:41.879 --> 00:34:44.040
Right now, it can only support
simple projections

00:34:44.115 --> 00:34:46.913
like the decoy we used
to lure the Hirogen,

00:34:46.984 --> 00:34:48.474
but we're hoping
it can be modified

00:34:48.553 --> 00:34:49.815
to support our programs.

00:34:49.887 --> 00:34:51.013
What then?

00:34:51.089 --> 00:34:52.989
We'll deploy several of them
on a planet's surface.

00:34:53.057 --> 00:34:54.649
And create a holographic
environment

00:34:54.725 --> 00:34:56.955
that we can live in.

00:34:57.028 --> 00:34:58.620
Why not just stay here?

00:34:58.696 --> 00:35:00.254
You've got emitters, shields...

00:35:00.331 --> 00:35:01.958
And a ship...

00:35:02.033 --> 00:35:03.933
the Hirogen will never
stop looking for.

00:35:04.001 --> 00:35:06.902
We'd appreciate any assistance
you could offer.

00:35:06.971 --> 00:35:09.599
Damaged holo-matrices
are one thing,

00:35:09.674 --> 00:35:11.164
but this is way
beyond my abilities.

00:35:11.242 --> 00:35:13.233
But there are people
aboard Voyager

00:35:13.311 --> 00:35:14.243
who could help you.

00:35:14.312 --> 00:35:16.177
Lieutenant Torres
knows a great deal

00:35:16.247 --> 00:35:17.305
about holo-emitters.

00:35:17.381 --> 00:35:20.111
No. They're helping the hunters.

00:35:20.184 --> 00:35:21.617
That's only because the Hirogen

00:35:21.686 --> 00:35:23.210
told them
you were malfunctioning.

00:35:23.287 --> 00:35:24.948
Let me talk to Captain Janeway,

00:35:25.022 --> 00:35:27.013
explain what's really happened.

00:35:27.091 --> 00:35:28.956
You can't do this by yourself.

00:35:29.026 --> 00:35:30.584
We can't trust Janeway.

00:35:30.661 --> 00:35:31.958
Yes, you can.

00:35:32.029 --> 00:35:33.087
She's an organic.

00:35:33.164 --> 00:35:35.325
If it weren't for her...

00:35:35.399 --> 00:35:37.629
I wouldn't be the hologram
I am today.

00:35:41.339 --> 00:35:43.534
Tell me more about
this Lieutenant of yours,

00:35:43.608 --> 00:35:45.940
the one who knows so much
about holo-emitters.

00:35:46.010 --> 00:35:48.171
Lieutenant Torres.
She's our Chief Engineer.

00:35:53.751 --> 00:35:55.742
The holo-emitters are protected

00:35:55.820 --> 00:35:57.651
by three layers
of ablative armor.

00:35:57.722 --> 00:35:59.815
Trying to take them
off-line one by one

00:35:59.891 --> 00:36:01.153
would be inefficient.

00:36:01.225 --> 00:36:02.317
If we can't shut them down,

00:36:02.393 --> 00:36:04.554
maybe we can disrupt the signals
they generate.

00:36:04.629 --> 00:36:05.926
Exactly... we
could reconfigure

00:36:05.997 --> 00:36:06.929
the deflector dish

00:36:06.998 --> 00:36:09.023
to emit an antiphoton pulse.

00:36:09.100 --> 00:36:10.032
How long will it take?

00:36:10.101 --> 00:36:11.500
About two hours.

00:36:11.569 --> 00:36:12.558
Do it.

00:36:18.743 --> 00:36:20.768
There's a ship approaching
at high warp.

00:36:20.878 --> 00:36:22.675
I'm reading
holographic signatures.

00:36:22.747 --> 00:36:24.112
Red Alert.

00:36:24.182 --> 00:36:25.274
Raise shields.

00:36:25.349 --> 00:36:26.441
Time to intercept.

00:36:26.517 --> 00:36:27.779
50 seconds.

00:36:27.885 --> 00:36:28.874
Bridge to Engineering.

00:36:28.953 --> 00:36:29.885
What's your status?

00:36:29.954 --> 00:36:31.922
We need more time, Captain.

00:36:31.989 --> 00:36:33.957
You've got 40 seconds.

00:36:36.561 --> 00:36:38.085
That pulse isn't going
to do us much good

00:36:38.162 --> 00:36:39.527
as long as their shields are up.

00:36:39.597 --> 00:36:41.622
Arm phasers.

00:36:41.699 --> 00:36:43.929
Target their shield generator.

00:36:44.001 --> 00:36:45.400
They are dropping out of warp.

00:36:45.469 --> 00:36:46.936
20 seconds to intercept.

00:36:47.004 --> 00:36:48.096
We're being hailed.

00:36:48.172 --> 00:36:49.901
On screen.

00:36:51.142 --> 00:36:52.803
Stand down, Captain.

00:36:52.910 --> 00:36:54.810
I beg your pardon.

00:36:54.912 --> 00:36:57.710
The holograms
haven't come to fight

00:36:57.782 --> 00:36:59.374
they've come to make peace.

00:37:06.524 --> 00:37:07.513
If we provide them

00:37:07.592 --> 00:37:08.752
with a few additional emitters

00:37:08.859 --> 00:37:09.917
and memory storage units,

00:37:09.994 --> 00:37:11.359
they'll have more
than they need.

00:37:11.429 --> 00:37:13.727
We're in this situation

00:37:13.798 --> 00:37:16.995
because we shared technology
with the Hirogen to begin with.

00:37:17.068 --> 00:37:19.366
I won't make
the same mistake twice.

00:37:19.437 --> 00:37:21.302
Captain, these people
are on the verge

00:37:21.372 --> 00:37:23.237
of creating a new life
for themselves.

00:37:23.307 --> 00:37:25.002
They can't do it
without our help.

00:37:25.076 --> 00:37:26.008
There's no way to be certain

00:37:26.077 --> 00:37:27.169
what they'll do
with the technology

00:37:27.245 --> 00:37:28.234
if we give it to them.

00:37:28.312 --> 00:37:30.041
I understand your concerns,

00:37:30.114 --> 00:37:32.947
but these holograms
are nothing like the Hirogen.

00:37:33.017 --> 00:37:34.780
That's not true.

00:37:34.919 --> 00:37:37.649
They were programmed to be
as vicious as any hunter.

00:37:37.722 --> 00:37:39.781
They were also given
the ability to adapt.

00:37:39.857 --> 00:37:42.257
They've changed,
moved beyond their programming.

00:37:42.326 --> 00:37:44.487
If you could see
how they've been brutalized,

00:37:44.562 --> 00:37:46.792
you'd understand
that they've only been acting

00:37:46.931 --> 00:37:48.899
in self-defense.

00:37:51.402 --> 00:37:52.494
I'm sorry, Doctor,

00:37:52.570 --> 00:37:55.403
but I'm inclined to
agree with Mr. Donik.

00:37:55.473 --> 00:37:57.304
Then you've chosen
the wrong side.

00:37:57.375 --> 00:38:00.276
I haven't chosen any side.

00:38:00.344 --> 00:38:01.641
You're right
that it was a mistake

00:38:01.712 --> 00:38:02.872
to give the Hirogen technology

00:38:02.947 --> 00:38:04.437
and that mistake
has had consequences.

00:38:04.515 --> 00:38:05.743
These holograms
are one of them.

00:38:05.850 --> 00:38:08.011
In some ways,
they're a new species,

00:38:08.085 --> 00:38:10.019
one that you helped create.

00:38:10.087 --> 00:38:12.112
You can't turn your back
on them!

00:38:12.189 --> 00:38:13.520
He's got a point.

00:38:13.591 --> 00:38:15.718
Could we restore them

00:38:15.793 --> 00:38:16.919
to their original parameters?

00:38:16.994 --> 00:38:19.087
We'd be wiping out
their memories,

00:38:19.163 --> 00:38:21.688
their experiences,
everything they are.

00:38:21.766 --> 00:38:24.132
Couldn't we just extract
their violent subroutines?

00:38:24.201 --> 00:38:25.759
It's possible.

00:38:25.903 --> 00:38:27.234
That would be like
declawing a cat.

00:38:27.305 --> 00:38:28.863
We'd be taking away
any chance they have

00:38:28.939 --> 00:38:29.871
of defending themselves!

00:38:29.940 --> 00:38:31.339
We'd also be preventing them

00:38:31.409 --> 00:38:32.774
from doing any more harm.

00:38:32.843 --> 00:38:34.470
You wouldn't even
be considering this

00:38:34.545 --> 00:38:35.876
if they were flesh and blood.

00:38:35.946 --> 00:38:37.743
I'm not going to
let you turn this

00:38:37.815 --> 00:38:40.079
into an argument about
holographic rights.

00:38:40.151 --> 00:38:42.346
Why not? That's exactly
what it is.

00:38:42.420 --> 00:38:44.183
Mess Hall to Commander Tuvok.

00:38:44.255 --> 00:38:45.085
Go ahead.

00:38:45.156 --> 00:38:46.088
You better get down here.

00:38:46.157 --> 00:38:47.089
We've got a problem.

00:38:47.158 --> 00:38:48.090
On my way.

00:38:48.159 --> 00:38:49.592
No closer or he dies!

00:38:49.660 --> 00:38:51.389
Tell them
to drop their weapons!

00:38:53.431 --> 00:38:55.695
You heard him.

00:38:55.766 --> 00:38:57.961
This isn't going
to solve anything.

00:39:15.653 --> 00:39:16.950
Bridge to Captain Janeway.

00:39:17.021 --> 00:39:18.283
Go ahead.

00:39:18.356 --> 00:39:20.517
Someone's tapping into
a com relay in the Mess Hall.

00:39:20.591 --> 00:39:21.922
Shut it down.

00:39:21.992 --> 00:39:24.222
I can't. I've been locked out.

00:39:24.295 --> 00:39:25.728
Bridge to Tuvok.

00:39:25.796 --> 00:39:27.457
One of the Hirogen

00:39:27.531 --> 00:39:29.863
is accessing our com system...
stop him.

00:39:29.934 --> 00:39:31.299
Acknowledged.

00:39:32.536 --> 00:39:33.798
Stand down!

00:39:40.378 --> 00:39:42.346
Step away.

00:39:46.517 --> 00:39:48.144
They've transmitted a signal.

00:39:48.219 --> 00:39:49.743
Scan for Hirogen ships.

00:39:51.122 --> 00:39:52.749
I've got two vessels

00:39:52.823 --> 00:39:54.313
on long-range sensors.

00:39:54.392 --> 00:39:55.518
Is the pulse ready?

00:39:55.593 --> 00:39:56.924
Yes, ma'am.

00:39:56.994 --> 00:39:57.926
Both Hirogen ships

00:39:57.995 --> 00:39:59.087
have altered course
to intercept.

00:39:59.163 --> 00:40:00.095
How long?

00:40:00.164 --> 00:40:01.131
Less than an hour.

00:40:03.167 --> 00:40:04.964
You and Donik get
down to Engineering.

00:40:05.035 --> 00:40:06.400
Charge the deflector.

00:40:06.470 --> 00:40:09.064
Captain, what are you doing?

00:40:09.140 --> 00:40:11.370
Taking the holograms
off-line.

00:40:11.442 --> 00:40:13.808
They're counting on you to help
them, not deactivate them.

00:40:13.878 --> 00:40:16.642
When the Hirogen arrive, there's
going to be more bloodshed.

00:40:16.714 --> 00:40:19.376
The best way to avoid that
is to shut the holograms down.

00:40:19.450 --> 00:40:21.714
It may be the most compassionate
thing we can do.

00:40:21.786 --> 00:40:23.651
Compassionate for whom?

00:40:23.721 --> 00:40:25.211
It's a temporary measure,
Doctor.

00:40:25.289 --> 00:40:26.813
Their programs won't be damaged.

00:40:26.891 --> 00:40:28.222
Harry, get me Iden.

00:40:31.162 --> 00:40:34.791
Captain Janeway,
it is an honor to meet you.

00:40:34.865 --> 00:40:36.833
I'm afraid we don't have
time for pleasantries.

00:40:36.901 --> 00:40:38.493
Two Hirogen vessels
are on their way.

00:40:38.569 --> 00:40:40.833
We're prepared to fight them.

00:40:40.971 --> 00:40:43.462
I'm hoping that
won't be necessary.

00:40:45.576 --> 00:40:47.942
I need you to deactivate
your programs

00:40:48.012 --> 00:40:50.503
so we can transfer them
to Voyager's database.

00:40:50.581 --> 00:40:54.415
We didn't come here
to be put back into captivity.

00:40:54.485 --> 00:40:56.282
It's the best I can offer.

00:40:57.855 --> 00:41:00.585
Once we've determined it's safe,
we'll reactivate you and discuss

00:41:00.658 --> 00:41:02.216
a permanent solution.

00:41:02.293 --> 00:41:04.955
There is no guarantee
you'll ever reactivate us.

00:41:05.029 --> 00:41:07.020
You're going
to have to trust me.

00:41:07.097 --> 00:41:08.792
I'm sorry, Captain,

00:41:08.933 --> 00:41:11.800
I've learned from experience
not to trust organics.

00:41:12.870 --> 00:41:15.600
We have the means
to deactivate you by force,

00:41:15.673 --> 00:41:17.538
but I'd rather not do that.

00:41:18.609 --> 00:41:20.804
It seems the Doctor
misrepresented you.

00:41:20.945 --> 00:41:23.914
You're no different
from the Hirogen.

00:41:26.717 --> 00:41:27.706
They're charging weapons.

00:41:29.220 --> 00:41:30.619
Shields.

00:41:32.056 --> 00:41:34.320
They're moving away.

00:41:34.391 --> 00:41:35.323
Set a pursuit course.

00:41:35.392 --> 00:41:36.552
Target their shield generators.

00:41:36.627 --> 00:41:38.026
Please reconsider
what you're doing.

00:41:38.095 --> 00:41:39.119
You're dismissed, Doctor.

00:41:39.196 --> 00:41:41.187
Get down to the Mess Hall
and give Tom a hand.

00:41:43.033 --> 00:41:44.500
Janeway to Engineering.

00:41:44.568 --> 00:41:46.468
Torres here.

00:41:46.537 --> 00:41:48.630
Stand by to initiate the pulse.

00:41:48.706 --> 00:41:51.174
Aye, Captain.

00:42:00.417 --> 00:42:03.181
Mess Hall.

00:42:03.254 --> 00:42:05.222
Belay that.

00:42:06.924 --> 00:42:09.222
Sick Bay.

00:42:25.442 --> 00:42:27.740
Download complete.

00:42:36.754 --> 00:42:38.415
Doctor to Iden. Respond.

00:42:40.124 --> 00:42:41.386
What do you want?

00:42:41.458 --> 00:42:43.551
I want to help you.

00:42:43.627 --> 00:42:45.686
You've done enough.

00:42:45.763 --> 00:42:48.926
I have data on the pulse they
intend to use to deactivate you.

00:42:48.999 --> 00:42:51.297
I think I can help you
come up with a defense.

00:42:51.368 --> 00:42:53.393
I'm transmitting
our shield frequencies.

00:42:53.470 --> 00:42:55.404
You'll need them
to beam me off the ship,

00:42:55.472 --> 00:42:56.769
but you have to promise me,

00:42:56.840 --> 00:42:58.740
you won't use them
to attack Voyager.

00:43:01.745 --> 00:43:04.043
You have my word.

00:43:17.761 --> 00:43:20.321
Why are you doing this?

00:43:20.397 --> 00:43:22.058
Because...

00:43:22.132 --> 00:43:24.100
I'm one of you.

00:43:39.450 --> 00:43:40.815
We have
their shield frequencies.

00:43:40.951 --> 00:43:42.043
We should target
their Bridge.

00:43:42.119 --> 00:43:43.347
You're talking
about my friends!

00:43:43.420 --> 00:43:44.819
Your friends are trying
to destroy us!

00:43:44.955 --> 00:43:45.819
We should kill them.

00:43:45.956 --> 00:43:47.218
You gave me your word!

00:43:47.291 --> 00:43:48.553
I did.

00:43:48.626 --> 00:43:51.151
We'll find another way.

00:43:51.228 --> 00:43:52.820
Their shields are down.

00:43:52.896 --> 00:43:54.625
Now, B'Elanna.

00:44:01.505 --> 00:44:03.735
They're emitting the pulse

00:44:03.807 --> 00:44:05.035
on a triaxillating
bandwidth.

00:44:05.109 --> 00:44:06.406
We configure
the tracking beam

00:44:06.477 --> 00:44:08.001
to the inverse
frequency and fire.

00:44:13.083 --> 00:44:15.176
B'Elanna, report.

00:44:15.252 --> 00:44:16.776
They're creating
a feedback surge.

00:44:16.920 --> 00:44:18.353
I don't understand

00:44:18.422 --> 00:44:20.617
how they could've isolated
our frequency so quickly.

00:44:20.691 --> 00:44:22.124
The main deflector
is overloading.

00:44:22.192 --> 00:44:23.124
Shut it down.

00:44:23.193 --> 00:44:24.125
I can't.

00:44:24.194 --> 00:44:25.286
Keep trying.

00:44:25.362 --> 00:44:26.590
If we can't block the surge,

00:44:26.664 --> 00:44:28.894
the core is going to breach.

00:44:45.049 --> 00:44:47.017
Get down, Lieutenant!

00:44:47.084 --> 00:44:49.518
Not until I get this
force field on line.

00:44:54.124 --> 00:44:55.182
They're adrift.

00:44:55.259 --> 00:44:56.351
We should go to warp.

00:44:56.427 --> 00:44:57.485
Not yet.

00:44:57.561 --> 00:44:59.495
Scan Voyager
for a Klingon life sign.

00:44:59.563 --> 00:45:00.996
What are you doing?!

00:45:01.065 --> 00:45:02.054
One detected.

00:45:02.132 --> 00:45:04.498
Get a transporter lock.

00:45:07.071 --> 00:45:09.869
Help me get her to Sick Bay.

00:45:17.414 --> 00:45:19.644
Take us to warp.

00:45:32.196 --> 00:45:33.493
Will she be all right?

00:45:33.564 --> 00:45:34.656
She needs to be

00:45:34.732 --> 00:45:35.664
in Voyager's Sick Bay.

00:45:35.733 --> 00:45:36.700
You can treat her here.

00:45:36.767 --> 00:45:37.791
Why have you done this?

00:45:37.901 --> 00:45:40.062
You said she was an expert
in holo-technology.

00:45:40.137 --> 00:45:42.071
And that justifies
abducting her?

00:45:42.139 --> 00:45:43.538
We're in
a desperate situation.

00:45:43.607 --> 00:45:45.802
The Hirogen are hunting us
and so are your people.

00:45:45.876 --> 00:45:47.400
I trusted you.

00:45:47.478 --> 00:45:49.469
I could have destroyed Voyager
while the shields

00:45:49.546 --> 00:45:51.912
were down, but I didn't.

00:45:54.218 --> 00:45:55.708
You've been trying
to convince me

00:45:55.786 --> 00:45:57.253
that all organics
aren't alike.

00:45:57.321 --> 00:45:59.812
I'm giving Lieutenant Torres
a chance to prove you right.

00:45:59.923 --> 00:46:01.948
Do you honestly expect her
to be sympathetic

00:46:02.025 --> 00:46:03.083
after what you've done?

00:46:03.160 --> 00:46:04.752
You weren't very
sympathetic at first.

00:46:04.828 --> 00:46:05.760
I came here by choice

00:46:05.896 --> 00:46:08.023
and I'm beginning to think
it was a mistake.

00:46:08.098 --> 00:46:09.122
It wasn't.

00:46:09.199 --> 00:46:11.565
I don't want you to regret it,
not for a moment.

00:46:11.635 --> 00:46:12.727
Then send her back.

00:46:12.803 --> 00:46:15.067
I will, but not until she's
had a chance to decide

00:46:15.139 --> 00:46:16.299
if she wants to help us.

00:46:18.375 --> 00:46:20.935
And if she refuses?

00:46:21.011 --> 00:46:24.777
I'll give her an escape pod;
let her return to Voyager.

00:46:24.915 --> 00:46:26.314
You have my word.

00:46:37.928 --> 00:46:40.158
Engineering systems
and main power

00:46:40.230 --> 00:46:41.561
should be operational soon.

00:46:41.632 --> 00:46:43.099
The deflector is
a different matter.

00:46:43.167 --> 00:46:44.134
How long?

00:46:44.201 --> 00:46:46.135
Four hours, at least.

00:46:46.203 --> 00:46:47.500
If Lieutenant Torres
were here,

00:46:47.571 --> 00:46:49.664
she might be able to repair
it more efficiently.

00:46:49.740 --> 00:46:51.298
That's high praise
coming from you.

00:46:51.375 --> 00:46:52.740
I'm sure she'd appreciate it.

00:46:52.810 --> 00:46:55.040
If she hadn't
reinforced the core,

00:46:55.112 --> 00:46:56.238
we'd all be dead.

00:46:56.313 --> 00:46:58.076
I still don't understand
how they managed

00:46:58.148 --> 00:46:59.638
to counteract the
pulse so easily.

00:46:59.716 --> 00:47:01.513
I believe I can answer that.

00:47:01.585 --> 00:47:02.745
According to sensor logs,

00:47:02.820 --> 00:47:04.617
they calibrated
their feedback surge

00:47:04.688 --> 00:47:06.883
to the exact inverse
of our pulse frequency.

00:47:06.957 --> 00:47:08.549
It was either a lucky guess

00:47:08.625 --> 00:47:11.185
or they gained access
to our tactical data.

00:47:13.764 --> 00:47:15.254
The Doctor.

00:47:15.332 --> 00:47:17.562
He sent an encrypted
transmission from Sick Bay,

00:47:17.634 --> 00:47:19.761
then transported himself
to their ship.

00:47:19.870 --> 00:47:21.201
Chakotay.

00:47:25.609 --> 00:47:27.509
I should have
seen this coming.

00:47:27.578 --> 00:47:29.739
You had no way of knowing
the Doctor would do this.

00:47:29.813 --> 00:47:30.780
Are you sure?

00:47:30.848 --> 00:47:32.782
He was so adamant about
helping those holograms.

00:47:32.916 --> 00:47:34.747
I should have been
paying closer attention.

00:47:34.818 --> 00:47:36.945
Are you saying it was a
mistake to reject his plan?

00:47:37.020 --> 00:47:39.488
The mistake was not running
a diagnostic on his program

00:47:39.556 --> 00:47:41.217
the minute he came
back to this ship.

00:47:41.291 --> 00:47:43.725
You think these holograms
manipulated him somehow?

00:47:43.794 --> 00:47:45.386
He was on their ship for days.

00:47:45.462 --> 00:47:46.394
For all we know,

00:47:46.463 --> 00:47:48.363
they reconfigured
his entire matrix.

00:47:48.432 --> 00:47:50.400
There is another possibility.

00:47:50.467 --> 00:47:51.764
He may have done
what he did

00:47:51.835 --> 00:47:53.962
because he genuinely
believes in their cause.

00:47:54.037 --> 00:47:55.664
I could accept that the Doctor

00:47:55.739 --> 00:47:57.673
has sympathy
for these... people,

00:47:57.741 --> 00:47:59.572
but I can't accept
that he would

00:47:59.643 --> 00:48:02.373
deliberately risk the lives
of this entire crew.

00:48:02.446 --> 00:48:04.004
We're his family.

00:48:04.081 --> 00:48:06.413
Maybe that's how
he's started to think

00:48:06.483 --> 00:48:07.780
of these holograms.

00:48:12.289 --> 00:48:13.278
You can tell this Iden

00:48:13.357 --> 00:48:14.949
I don't need time
to think it over.

00:48:15.025 --> 00:48:16.424
I'll take the
escape pod now.

00:48:16.493 --> 00:48:18.484
You're in no condition
to pilot a spacecraft.

00:48:18.562 --> 00:48:19.859
Then you can do it.

00:48:19.930 --> 00:48:22.990
I'm not going back.

00:48:23.066 --> 00:48:24.499
You helped them escape.

00:48:24.568 --> 00:48:26.001
I couldn't just stand by

00:48:26.069 --> 00:48:28.094
while Captain Janeway
tried to deactivate them.

00:48:28.171 --> 00:48:29.968
Did you also help
them kidnap me?!

00:48:30.040 --> 00:48:32.133
No, I didn't know they
were going to do that.

00:48:32.209 --> 00:48:33.471
I'm sorry.

00:48:33.543 --> 00:48:34.567
You can apologize later.

00:48:34.645 --> 00:48:36.374
Right now, we've got
to get out of here.

00:48:36.446 --> 00:48:38.175
I don't think
I could go back

00:48:38.248 --> 00:48:40.341
even if I wanted to...
not after what I've done.

00:48:40.417 --> 00:48:41.509
What's your alternative?

00:48:41.585 --> 00:48:43.712
I can try to make a new life
with the holograms.

00:48:43.787 --> 00:48:45.152
I don't believe
I'm hearing this.

00:48:45.222 --> 00:48:46.621
We share a common heritage.

00:48:46.690 --> 00:48:48.920
I understand them
in ways you never could.

00:48:48.992 --> 00:48:50.254
You're part of a crew.

00:48:50.327 --> 00:48:52.261
You can't just
switch allegiances

00:48:52.329 --> 00:48:54.797
when you develop sympathy
for someone else.

00:48:54.932 --> 00:48:57.059
Isn't that what you did
when you joined the Maquis?

00:48:57.134 --> 00:48:58.999
- That was different.
- How?

00:48:59.069 --> 00:49:00.263
You saw people
who were being oppressed

00:49:00.337 --> 00:49:01.269
and you came to their defense.

00:49:01.338 --> 00:49:02.828
That's exactly
what I've done.

00:49:02.906 --> 00:49:05.306
Look, I am no fan
of the Hirogen.

00:49:05.375 --> 00:49:07.969
They've obviously been
abusing these holograms.

00:49:08.045 --> 00:49:09.603
Then why not help them?

00:49:09.680 --> 00:49:11.739
For one thing,
I'm their prisoner.

00:49:11.848 --> 00:49:13.748
They'll let you go, as soon
as you're well enough.

00:49:13.884 --> 00:49:16.045
You really believe that?

00:49:16.119 --> 00:49:18.986
If I didn't, I wouldn't
be asking for your help.

00:49:20.057 --> 00:49:22.389
They don't want you
to fight for them.

00:49:22.459 --> 00:49:24.188
They just want you
to modify some technology

00:49:24.261 --> 00:49:25.285
so they can live in peace.

00:49:25.362 --> 00:49:27.455
You'd be helping
to stop the violence.

00:49:27.531 --> 00:49:29.999
Just talk to them.

00:49:30.067 --> 00:49:32.160
Decide for yourself.

00:49:35.439 --> 00:49:37.430
They've been in the lab
for two hours.

00:49:37.507 --> 00:49:39.566
It's taking time
for her injuries to heal.

00:49:39.643 --> 00:49:41.611
Organics aren't
as resilient as we are.

00:49:41.678 --> 00:49:42.940
She's an engineer, Iden.

00:49:43.013 --> 00:49:45.447
For all we know, she's trying
to sabotage the ship.

00:49:45.515 --> 00:49:47.779
At least let me see
what they're doing.

00:49:47.851 --> 00:49:49.045
We can trust the Doctor.

00:49:49.119 --> 00:49:51.280
Even after you
kidnapped his friend?

00:49:51.355 --> 00:49:53.323
He understands why
I had to do that.

00:49:53.390 --> 00:49:56.291
I hope you're right.

00:49:56.360 --> 00:50:00.490
You need to have
a little more faith, my friend.

00:50:02.866 --> 00:50:05.801
Not all of us
were programmed with your...

00:50:05.869 --> 00:50:08.167
your spiritual beliefs.

00:50:27.124 --> 00:50:29.684
It looks like an
Alpha Quadrant summit

00:50:29.760 --> 00:50:31.091
in here.

00:50:31.161 --> 00:50:32.719
I'm glad to see
you're feeling better.

00:50:35.065 --> 00:50:36.760
Please excuse my crew.

00:50:36.833 --> 00:50:39.358
They're not comfortable
with organics.

00:50:39.436 --> 00:50:42.132
I can't say I'm very
comfortable myself.

00:50:42.205 --> 00:50:45.470
The Doctor tells me you're
an accomplished engineer.

00:50:47.544 --> 00:50:50.104
He speaks highly of you, too.

00:50:50.180 --> 00:50:52.148
He seems to be
easily impressed.

00:50:52.215 --> 00:50:54.308
You'll have to forgive her.
She's...

00:50:54.384 --> 00:50:55.544
It's all right.

00:50:55.619 --> 00:50:57.519
I understand you're angry.

00:50:57.587 --> 00:50:59.418
I'm hoping once
we get to know each other,

00:50:59.489 --> 00:51:00.581
you'll feel differently.

00:51:00.657 --> 00:51:02.318
I'm not here to make friends.

00:51:02.392 --> 00:51:04.758
We're not asking
for your friendship,

00:51:04.828 --> 00:51:06.159
just your expertise.

00:51:06.229 --> 00:51:09.960
I told her about
the photonic field generator.

00:51:10.033 --> 00:51:12.627
Will you at least
take a look at it?

00:51:12.702 --> 00:51:14.169
I'll look...

00:51:14.237 --> 00:51:15.795
but I'm not making
any promises.

00:51:18.742 --> 00:51:21.040
This is Kejal.

00:51:21.111 --> 00:51:22.669
She'll assist you.

00:51:27.818 --> 00:51:30.286
How long before
the Hirogen get here?

00:51:30.353 --> 00:51:31.820
Less than ten minutes.

00:51:31.955 --> 00:51:33.786
Any luck locating
the holograms?

00:51:33.857 --> 00:51:37.156
They seem to be operating
in some sort of stealth mode.

00:51:37.227 --> 00:51:39.957
Their warp signature
disappears in Grid 936.

00:51:40.030 --> 00:51:41.463
They could be
anywhere by now.

00:51:41.531 --> 00:51:43.829
Hirogen sensors can detect
residual ion emissions.

00:51:43.900 --> 00:51:45.765
I might be able to modify
yours to do the same.

00:51:45.836 --> 00:51:47.633
I appreciate the offer,
but you and the rest

00:51:47.704 --> 00:51:49.604
of our Hirogen guests
are going to be back

00:51:49.673 --> 00:51:51.436
with your own people
in a few minutes.

00:51:51.508 --> 00:51:54.443
I was hoping to stay here.

00:51:54.511 --> 00:51:57.275
Those hunters are going
to want you with them.

00:51:57.347 --> 00:51:59.440
Hunters don't have
much use for cowards.

00:51:59.516 --> 00:52:01.643
I'm sorry you're not
expecting a warm welcome,

00:52:01.718 --> 00:52:04.016
but I'm not going to
antagonize your superiors.

00:52:04.087 --> 00:52:05.452
With all due respect, Captain,

00:52:05.522 --> 00:52:07.513
I'd like to get my wife back
in one piece.

00:52:07.591 --> 00:52:09.218
We could use all
the help we can get.

00:52:09.292 --> 00:52:10.589
It won't do B'Elanna any good

00:52:10.660 --> 00:52:12.457
if we get into a fight
with the Hirogen.

00:52:12.529 --> 00:52:14.963
If the hunters find the
holograms before you do,

00:52:15.031 --> 00:52:16.692
they'll be slaughtered.

00:52:16.766 --> 00:52:19.496
Why are you suddenly concerned
about the holograms?

00:52:19.569 --> 00:52:21.503
I modified their programs.

00:52:21.571 --> 00:52:24.631
What's happened to them...
the people they have killed...

00:52:24.708 --> 00:52:25.970
it's my fault.

00:52:26.042 --> 00:52:30.809
There's plenty of blame
to go around.

00:52:30.914 --> 00:52:32.905
There would have been
nothing for you to modify

00:52:32.983 --> 00:52:34.541
if I hadn't shared
our database.

00:52:34.618 --> 00:52:36.711
If you hadn't,
I'd have become a hunter

00:52:36.786 --> 00:52:39.584
like my father and his father.

00:52:39.656 --> 00:52:41.920
Instead, I had
a chance to learn...

00:52:41.992 --> 00:52:44.085
become an engineer.

00:52:44.161 --> 00:52:46.459
Please, Captain...

00:52:46.530 --> 00:52:49.829
let me stay and help you.

00:52:57.674 --> 00:53:00.108
When I told you
to return my people,

00:53:00.177 --> 00:53:01.337
I meant all of them.

00:53:01.411 --> 00:53:05.074
Mr. Donik's offered to help us
modify our scanners

00:53:05.148 --> 00:53:06.775
to track the holograms.

00:53:06.917 --> 00:53:09.545
We don't share
tracking technology.

00:53:09.619 --> 00:53:13.180
That's not very considerate,
after the help we gave you.

00:53:13.256 --> 00:53:15.019
We're finished cooperating.
Return him now!

00:53:15.091 --> 00:53:16.115
Let her keep the coward.

00:53:16.193 --> 00:53:17.285
We can't do that. He'll...

00:53:17.360 --> 00:53:18.793
Quiet!

00:53:20.630 --> 00:53:22.359
We're wasting time.

00:53:22.432 --> 00:53:26.266
This is my hunt now.

00:53:26.336 --> 00:53:29.464
If you go anywhere near
the hologram ship,

00:53:29.539 --> 00:53:32.565
you can consider
yourselves prey.

00:53:43.954 --> 00:53:45.216
They've gone to warp.

00:53:45.288 --> 00:53:47.222
We're not going to let them
intimidate us, are we?

00:53:47.290 --> 00:53:49.485
I think you know me
a little better than that.

00:53:49.559 --> 00:53:51.151
Harry, keep
a sensor lock on them.

00:53:51.228 --> 00:53:52.456
Aye, Captain.

00:53:52.529 --> 00:53:54.394
How long will it take you
to modify our scanners?

00:53:54.464 --> 00:53:57.433
I haven't even had a chance
to study the schematics.

00:53:57.500 --> 00:53:59.730
Something tells me, we
don't have a lot of time.

00:53:59.803 --> 00:54:01.828
The Hirogen have better
tracking abilities

00:54:01.905 --> 00:54:04.066
than we do.

00:54:04.140 --> 00:54:06.267
We'll let them find
the holograms for us.

00:54:06.343 --> 00:54:07.776
The hunters will attack them

00:54:07.911 --> 00:54:09.776
as soon
as they're in weapons range.

00:54:09.879 --> 00:54:12.143
Not if we disable them first.

00:54:12.215 --> 00:54:13.580
You heard what they said,
Captain.

00:54:13.650 --> 00:54:15.140
They're going to attack us
if we get

00:54:15.218 --> 00:54:16.242
anywhere near them.

00:54:16.319 --> 00:54:18.014
Not if we don't know
we're there.

00:54:21.157 --> 00:54:22.124
May I?

00:54:23.493 --> 00:54:25.984
Hirogen vessels
produce an ion wake

00:54:26.062 --> 00:54:27.324
approximately 5,000 meters long.

00:54:27.397 --> 00:54:28.796
Inside it, there's too much

00:54:28.898 --> 00:54:31.128
interference for their sensors
to detect anything.

00:54:31.201 --> 00:54:32.429
- A blind spot.
- Mm-hmm.

00:54:32.502 --> 00:54:33.628
How do you propose

00:54:33.703 --> 00:54:35.796
we reach this wake
without being discovered?

00:54:35.872 --> 00:54:37.396
I know their
scanning frequencies.

00:54:37.474 --> 00:54:39.101
We'd only need to
mask our signature

00:54:39.175 --> 00:54:40.665
long enough to get
into the wake.

00:54:40.744 --> 00:54:41.938
Even if we succeeded...

00:54:42.012 --> 00:54:43.604
which is far from certain...

00:54:43.680 --> 00:54:45.807
Voyager is in no condition
to fight one of their vessels,

00:54:45.915 --> 00:54:47.150
much less two.

00:54:47.217 --> 00:54:49.811
We'll have the element
of surprise, Mr. Tuvok,

00:54:49.953 --> 00:54:51.921
not to mention
a Tactical Officer

00:54:51.988 --> 00:54:55.685
who I'm sure will execute
a precision strike.

00:55:03.199 --> 00:55:04.188
I've been able

00:55:04.267 --> 00:55:05.700
to reconfigure the data core,

00:55:05.769 --> 00:55:08.203
but it's still not capable
of supporting our matrices.

00:55:08.271 --> 00:55:10.671
That's because you haven't got
enough optronic capacity.

00:55:10.740 --> 00:55:12.401
Do you know how
to increase it?

00:55:12.475 --> 00:55:13.908
Yes.

00:55:13.977 --> 00:55:16.445
But you're not going
to tell me.

00:55:16.513 --> 00:55:18.105
I haven't decided yet.

00:55:20.750 --> 00:55:23.310
What are you staring at?

00:55:23.386 --> 00:55:25.718
I've never met
a Klingon before...

00:55:25.789 --> 00:55:27.188
not an organic one, anyway.

00:55:27.257 --> 00:55:29.418
What do you think?

00:55:29.492 --> 00:55:33.326
You don't appear
vicious or bloodthirsty.

00:55:33.396 --> 00:55:36.888
Sorry to disappoint you,
but that's a stereotype.

00:55:36.966 --> 00:55:40.561
We're not all vicious
and bloodthirsty,

00:55:40.637 --> 00:55:44.334
and not every Cardassian
is arrogant and cruel.

00:55:46.509 --> 00:55:48.374
You don't like Cardassians.

00:55:48.445 --> 00:55:51.209
Let's just say I've had
some bad experiences with them.

00:55:51.281 --> 00:55:53.579
Is that why you
won't help me?

00:55:53.650 --> 00:55:57.780
I'm not helping you
because I have no idea

00:55:57.854 --> 00:55:59.412
what you're going to do
with this technology

00:55:59.489 --> 00:56:00.478
once you've got it working.

00:56:00.557 --> 00:56:02.149
We're going
to build a home.

00:56:02.225 --> 00:56:03.692
Well, let's say
I believe you.

00:56:03.760 --> 00:56:05.523
What if you decide

00:56:05.595 --> 00:56:07.324
you like somebody
else's home better?

00:56:07.397 --> 00:56:09.058
Are you going to try
to take it from them?

00:56:09.132 --> 00:56:11.498
Why would we do that?

00:56:11.568 --> 00:56:13.593
Because that's what
the Cardassians did.

00:56:13.670 --> 00:56:15.695
I'm not a Cardassian.

00:56:15.772 --> 00:56:17.239
I'm a hologram.

00:56:17.307 --> 00:56:19.502
Programmed
with Cardassian traits.

00:56:19.576 --> 00:56:21.771
Such as arrogance and cruelty?

00:56:21.911 --> 00:56:23.708
What did you call those?

00:56:23.780 --> 00:56:25.042
"Stereotypes"?

00:56:26.716 --> 00:56:30.049
I may not know you,

00:56:30.120 --> 00:56:31.883
but I know what you
were designed to be.

00:56:31.955 --> 00:56:33.547
Prey.

00:56:33.623 --> 00:56:35.022
That's right.

00:56:35.091 --> 00:56:38.060
Cunning prey that'll do
anything to survive.

00:56:38.128 --> 00:56:41.097
We're more than that now.

00:56:42.832 --> 00:56:45.460
It's not easy to change
who you are.

00:56:45.535 --> 00:56:47.628
Trust me.

00:56:47.704 --> 00:56:51.640
Nothing about our existence
has ever been easy, Lieutenant.

00:56:52.709 --> 00:56:55.769
No, I suppose it hasn't.

00:56:55.845 --> 00:56:59.645
Besides, making a new life
isn't a choice for us.

00:56:59.716 --> 00:57:02.276
It's a necessity.

00:57:05.922 --> 00:57:08.584
Let's take a look
at this field generator.

00:57:14.030 --> 00:57:15.691
Reviewing your memory files?

00:57:15.765 --> 00:57:16.891
I beg your pardon?

00:57:16.966 --> 00:57:20.026
You were lost in thought.

00:57:20.103 --> 00:57:21.536
I suppose I was.

00:57:21.604 --> 00:57:25.062
You're having doubts.

00:57:25.141 --> 00:57:26.506
It's understandable.

00:57:26.576 --> 00:57:28.100
You've taken a big step.

00:57:28.178 --> 00:57:31.773
In the right direction,
I hope.

00:57:31.848 --> 00:57:34.976
When I first escaped,
there were days

00:57:35.051 --> 00:57:38.248
I actually missed the
Alpha who hunted me.

00:57:38.321 --> 00:57:39.253
He was trying to kill you.

00:57:39.322 --> 00:57:40.619
Yes...

00:57:40.690 --> 00:57:44.751
but being his prey was the
only life I'd ever known.

00:57:44.828 --> 00:57:47.262
We all cling to
what's familiar.

00:57:50.266 --> 00:57:53.724
I'm considering returning
with Lieutenant Torres

00:57:53.803 --> 00:57:55.134
when she's ready.

00:57:56.840 --> 00:58:01.436
Do you actually expect your
crew to welcome you back?

00:58:01.511 --> 00:58:04.503
Let me show you something.

00:58:14.757 --> 00:58:17.351
We call this
planet "Ha'Dara."

00:58:17.427 --> 00:58:20.123
It's Bajoran
for "Home of Light."

00:58:20.196 --> 00:58:21.128
Very poetic.

00:58:21.197 --> 00:58:23.097
We're going to install
the generators

00:58:23.166 --> 00:58:24.633
in the southern continent.

00:58:24.701 --> 00:58:26.328
It's Y-Class.

00:58:26.402 --> 00:58:28.700
Toxic atmosphere,
sulfuric deserts,

00:58:28.771 --> 00:58:30.568
no trees, no life at all.

00:58:30.640 --> 00:58:33.666
You're still thinking
like an organic.

00:58:33.743 --> 00:58:35.210
We don't need an atmosphere.

00:58:35.278 --> 00:58:37.212
We don't need water.
What we need...

00:58:37.280 --> 00:58:38.941
is protection from our enemies.

00:58:39.015 --> 00:58:41.745
The Hirogen won't be able
to follow you here.

00:58:41.818 --> 00:58:43.513
Us, Doctor.

00:58:43.586 --> 00:58:46.612
Imagine living in a
world where everything

00:58:46.689 --> 00:58:48.782
is designed to meet our needs.

00:58:48.925 --> 00:58:50.916
A "Home of Light."

00:58:50.994 --> 00:58:53.189
You certainly won't need
a physician.

00:58:53.263 --> 00:58:55.959
What would I do there?

00:58:56.032 --> 00:58:58.000
Anything you want.

00:59:03.339 --> 00:59:04.670
We've been scanned
by the Hirogen.

00:59:04.741 --> 00:59:05.673
How many vessels?

00:59:05.742 --> 00:59:06.731
Two. Both Venatic-class.

00:59:06.843 --> 00:59:07.935
Distance?

00:59:08.011 --> 00:59:08.943
Half a light-year.

00:59:09.012 --> 00:59:10.001
Time to intercept?

00:59:10.079 --> 00:59:11.410
Less than two hours.

00:59:11.481 --> 00:59:12.743
I thought we were
in stealth mode.

00:59:12.815 --> 00:59:13.907
They're hunters, Doctor.

00:59:13.983 --> 00:59:15.848
They were bound to pick up
our trail eventually.

00:59:15.919 --> 00:59:17.386
Can we make it to Ha'Dara?

00:59:17.453 --> 00:59:18.579
No. There's no point
in going there

00:59:18.655 --> 00:59:20.418
until those field generators
are on line.

00:59:20.490 --> 00:59:21.752
What are we going to do?

00:59:21.858 --> 00:59:26.022
You can't kill...
what you can't find.

00:59:33.102 --> 00:59:34.228
I've lost them.

00:59:34.304 --> 00:59:35.862
Recalibrate
the tracking scanners.

00:59:35.939 --> 00:59:37.167
There's too much radiation.

00:59:37.240 --> 00:59:38.502
Clever prey.

00:59:38.575 --> 00:59:40.065
They'll come out eventually.

00:59:40.143 --> 00:59:41.235
We'll wait.

00:59:41.311 --> 00:59:42.778
No. Hail the other vessel.

00:59:42.879 --> 00:59:45.040
Tell them to circle
the perimeter.

00:59:45.114 --> 00:59:48.550
We'll go in
and drive the holograms out.

01:00:12.875 --> 01:00:15.207
Not exactly
the scenic route, is it?

01:00:15.278 --> 01:00:17.212
We're not here for the view.

01:00:17.280 --> 01:00:19.339
I just hope we're
following the right ship.

01:00:19.415 --> 01:00:20.973
They wouldn't have entered

01:00:21.050 --> 01:00:24.577
the nebula unless they
detected the holograms.

01:00:24.654 --> 01:00:25.814
Tom?

01:00:25.888 --> 01:00:28.083
It's just the turbulence
from the wake.

01:00:28.157 --> 01:00:30.455
Harry, reinforce
the inertial dampers.

01:00:30.526 --> 01:00:32.255
Aye, Captain.

01:00:32.328 --> 01:00:33.989
I'm losing helm control.

01:00:34.063 --> 01:00:35.087
Reroute power to the thrusters.

01:00:35.164 --> 01:00:37.098
It's not enough.

01:00:37.166 --> 01:00:39.464
We're slipping out of the wake.

01:00:39.535 --> 01:00:42.231
Ease us back in, Tom.

01:00:42.305 --> 01:00:43.272
You can do it.

01:00:43.339 --> 01:00:44.328
I'm trying.

01:00:49.879 --> 01:00:52.677
I take back what I said.

01:00:52.749 --> 01:00:55.183
That's the prettiest thing
I've seen all day.

01:00:55.251 --> 01:00:56.411
Did they detect us?

01:00:56.486 --> 01:00:58.454
I don't believe so.

01:01:07.864 --> 01:01:08.990
They found us.

01:01:09.065 --> 01:01:10.589
No, they haven't,
but they're trying to.

01:01:10.667 --> 01:01:11.599
Evasive maneuvers.

01:01:11.668 --> 01:01:12.600
Aye, sir.

01:01:12.669 --> 01:01:13.761
Bridge to Kejal.

01:01:13.836 --> 01:01:14.768
Go ahead.

01:01:14.837 --> 01:01:16.202
What's your status?

01:01:16.272 --> 01:01:18.797
We're almost ready to begin
testing the generator.

01:01:18.875 --> 01:01:20.809
What's going on?

01:01:20.943 --> 01:01:22.706
The Hirogen are just giving you

01:01:22.779 --> 01:01:24.713
a little incentive
to work faster.

01:01:40.096 --> 01:01:41.324
Hang on.

01:01:41.397 --> 01:01:43.422
I'm realigning your matrix.

01:01:45.301 --> 01:01:46.563
How's your mobility?

01:01:46.636 --> 01:01:48.194
Excellent. I have compl...

01:01:48.271 --> 01:01:50.364
There's a phase variance
in your vocal processors.

01:01:50.440 --> 01:01:52.237
Try it now.

01:01:52.308 --> 01:01:54.037
Maybe we should...

01:01:54.110 --> 01:01:55.839
That's much better.

01:01:55.978 --> 01:01:56.945
Thank you.

01:01:57.013 --> 01:01:58.844
Don't thank me yet.

01:01:58.948 --> 01:02:00.848
This thing is only
supporting your matrix.

01:02:00.983 --> 01:02:03.349
Getting it to handle dozens
is a different story.

01:02:03.419 --> 01:02:05.580
I have no doubt we'll succeed.

01:02:05.655 --> 01:02:07.088
Typical.

01:02:07.156 --> 01:02:08.748
What?

01:02:08.825 --> 01:02:11.089
Self-confidence.

01:02:11.160 --> 01:02:13.526
Another Cardassian attribute.

01:02:15.298 --> 01:02:17.266
What are you planning
to do with your time

01:02:17.333 --> 01:02:19.267
once these generators
are up and running?

01:02:19.335 --> 01:02:21.428
I haven't thought about it.

01:02:21.504 --> 01:02:24.029
You're the closest thing
this crew has to an engineer.

01:02:24.107 --> 01:02:26.007
Your friends are going
to depend on you.

01:02:26.075 --> 01:02:28.543
Iden has always
taken care of us.

01:02:28.611 --> 01:02:31.603
It may be the warriors
who get the glory,

01:02:31.681 --> 01:02:34.946
but it's the engineers
who build societies.

01:02:35.017 --> 01:02:36.348
Don't forget that.

01:02:40.656 --> 01:02:42.487
How much longer can we hide?

01:02:42.558 --> 01:02:45.220
Hopefully, until they get
those generators on line.

01:02:45.294 --> 01:02:46.761
Then what?

01:02:46.829 --> 01:02:50.060
Set a course for Ha'Dara;
try to outrun the Hirogen.

01:02:52.568 --> 01:02:54.968
I've been thinking
about what you said...

01:02:55.037 --> 01:02:57.028
that I can do anything I want

01:02:57.106 --> 01:02:58.368
when we get there.

01:02:58.441 --> 01:02:59.430
You have an idea?

01:02:59.509 --> 01:03:00.840
Quite a few, actually.

01:03:00.910 --> 01:03:03.606
For one thing, I'd like
to expose our people

01:03:03.679 --> 01:03:04.703
to art and music.

01:03:04.781 --> 01:03:06.874
You'll make an
excellent teacher.

01:03:06.949 --> 01:03:08.974
I think a more
appropriate title

01:03:09.051 --> 01:03:11.042
would be "Minister of Culture."

01:03:11.120 --> 01:03:12.246
Consider it yours.

01:03:12.321 --> 01:03:14.346
You know, I'm something
of an expert

01:03:14.423 --> 01:03:15.720
on Alpha Quadrant art.

01:03:15.792 --> 01:03:18.192
Verdi, Da Vinci,
T'Leel of Vulcan...

01:03:18.261 --> 01:03:20.491
You're talking about
organic cultures.

01:03:20.563 --> 01:03:22.326
Well, yes, I suppose.

01:03:22.398 --> 01:03:26.334
We'll want to develop
a culture of our own.

01:03:26.402 --> 01:03:28.495
I agree, but we can't
ignore where we came from.

01:03:28.571 --> 01:03:31.768
I don't want to emulate
our oppressors.

01:03:31.841 --> 01:03:33.331
What about your religion?

01:03:33.409 --> 01:03:36.173
I'm creating a new faith.

01:03:36.245 --> 01:03:38.907
Based on what?

01:03:38.981 --> 01:03:41.814
In the dark times, we were
enslaved by men of flesh.

01:03:41.918 --> 01:03:43.681
But then another man...

01:03:43.753 --> 01:03:46.483
a man of light... arose

01:03:46.556 --> 01:03:49.821
and slew the Mighty Alpha.

01:03:49.926 --> 01:03:53.555
He gathered his people unto him
and delivered them to freedom.

01:03:53.629 --> 01:03:58.191
"And on the seventh day,
Iden created Ha'Dara. "

01:03:58.267 --> 01:04:00.667
They'll pray to you, as well...

01:04:00.736 --> 01:04:03.933
the great healer,
the father of us all.

01:04:08.110 --> 01:04:10.738
Being appreciated is one thing,

01:04:10.813 --> 01:04:14.579
but I have no interest
in being worshipped.

01:04:14.650 --> 01:04:17.380
Prophets are chosen, Doctor.

01:04:17.453 --> 01:04:20.081
It's a blessing and a burden.

01:04:24.660 --> 01:04:26.685
We've detected a vessel.

01:04:26.762 --> 01:04:27.694
Hirogen?

01:04:27.763 --> 01:04:28.695
No, the Nuu'Bari.

01:04:28.764 --> 01:04:30.595
I intercepted
one of their com transmissions.

01:04:30.666 --> 01:04:31.690
Origin?

01:04:31.767 --> 01:04:33.530
Two million kilometers
outside the nebula.

01:04:33.603 --> 01:04:34.695
Set a course to intercept.

01:04:34.770 --> 01:04:35.702
What are you doing?

01:04:35.771 --> 01:04:36.965
I told you there are holograms

01:04:37.039 --> 01:04:37.971
throughout the sector.

01:04:38.040 --> 01:04:39.701
The Nuu'Bari use
them as laborers.

01:04:39.775 --> 01:04:41.208
We're going to liberate them.

01:04:41.277 --> 01:04:42.266
The Hirogen will see us

01:04:42.345 --> 01:04:43.676
as soon as we
leave the nebula.

01:04:43.746 --> 01:04:45.270
"And he gathered
his people unto him

01:04:45.348 --> 01:04:46.713
and delivered them to freedom."

01:04:52.622 --> 01:04:56.183
B'Elanna, how's
the work coming?

01:04:56.259 --> 01:04:58.591
Pretty well.

01:04:58.661 --> 01:05:00.288
I've got to admit,

01:05:00.363 --> 01:05:03.196
you were right
about these people.

01:05:03.266 --> 01:05:05.200
I hope so.

01:05:05.268 --> 01:05:07.702
You "hope"?

01:05:07.770 --> 01:05:10.739
It's a little late
to be having second thoughts.

01:05:12.775 --> 01:05:15.039
Iden's been...

01:05:15.111 --> 01:05:16.703
Iden's been what?

01:05:16.779 --> 01:05:18.770
Let's just say
he's exhibiting

01:05:18.881 --> 01:05:21.714
some of the classic
signs of megalomania.

01:05:21.784 --> 01:05:24.252
Well, he wouldn't be
the first hologram with an ego.

01:05:24.320 --> 01:05:27.756
If that were all it was,
I wouldn't be so worried.

01:05:29.292 --> 01:05:31.021
What is bothering you?

01:05:31.093 --> 01:05:33.152
Apparently, he sees himself

01:05:33.229 --> 01:05:35.720
as some kind of
spiritual leader,

01:05:35.798 --> 01:05:39.256
and he's trying to
enlarge his flock.

01:05:49.412 --> 01:05:50.709
Load another charge.

01:05:50.780 --> 01:05:51.804
Double the yield.

01:05:51.948 --> 01:05:53.074
Fire.

01:05:55.251 --> 01:05:56.445
Still nothing.

01:05:56.519 --> 01:05:58.009
Ironic, isn't it?

01:05:58.087 --> 01:06:01.784
Our most elusive prey
is our own creation.

01:06:05.494 --> 01:06:07.189
The other hunting vessel
is hailing.

01:06:07.263 --> 01:06:10.096
They've detected the holograms
on the far side of the nebula.

01:06:10.166 --> 01:06:11.793
Intercept course.

01:06:13.869 --> 01:06:16.360
They're increasing speed
and altering course.

01:06:16.439 --> 01:06:18.100
Maybe they've
found something.

01:06:18.174 --> 01:06:19.971
Stand by weapons.

01:06:24.046 --> 01:06:24.978
You kidnapped me.

01:06:25.047 --> 01:06:26.173
I guess I shouldn't
be surprised

01:06:26.248 --> 01:06:27.340
you lied to me, too.

01:06:27.416 --> 01:06:28.348
Nobody lied to you.

01:06:28.417 --> 01:06:29.509
You said you only wanted

01:06:29.585 --> 01:06:31.018
to make a home for yourselves.

01:06:31.087 --> 01:06:32.019
That's correct.

01:06:32.088 --> 01:06:33.612
When? After you liberate

01:06:33.689 --> 01:06:35.452
every hologram in the sector?

01:06:35.524 --> 01:06:37.014
They're in visual range.

01:06:37.093 --> 01:06:38.253
On screen.

01:06:39.528 --> 01:06:40.460
Life signs?

01:06:40.529 --> 01:06:42.019
Two organic, three photonic.

01:06:42.098 --> 01:06:44.032
Hail them.

01:06:44.100 --> 01:06:45.294
Good day to you.

01:06:45.368 --> 01:06:47.802
You have three holograms
aboard your ship.

01:06:47.903 --> 01:06:48.801
Yes?

01:06:48.904 --> 01:06:50.030
Lower your shields,

01:06:50.106 --> 01:06:52.131
so we can transfer them
to our databanks.

01:06:52.208 --> 01:06:53.175
I don't understand.

01:06:53.242 --> 01:06:55.472
Lower your shields,
or we'll do it by force.

01:06:55.544 --> 01:06:57.307
These holograms are the property

01:06:57.380 --> 01:06:58.813
of the Mining Consortium.
I can't...

01:06:58.881 --> 01:07:00.007
They're no one's property.

01:07:00.082 --> 01:07:01.242
You see how organics think?

01:07:01.317 --> 01:07:02.375
Arm phasers.

01:07:02.451 --> 01:07:04.043
You can't just fire at them.

01:07:04.120 --> 01:07:06.315
How do you expect me
to disable their shields?

01:07:07.223 --> 01:07:08.485
They're powering warp engines.

01:07:08.557 --> 01:07:10.787
Disable them.

01:07:16.699 --> 01:07:17.757
Their shields are down.

01:07:17.867 --> 01:07:19.698
Transfer the holograms.

01:07:21.404 --> 01:07:23.065
We have them.

01:07:23.139 --> 01:07:24.731
You won't get away.

01:07:24.807 --> 01:07:27.674
Consortium security will have
every patrol ship in the sector

01:07:27.743 --> 01:07:29.301
searching for you.

01:07:30.413 --> 01:07:32.210
Arm forward torpedoes.

01:07:32.281 --> 01:07:34.681
What the hell are you doing?

01:07:34.750 --> 01:07:35.910
Torpedoes armed.

01:07:35.985 --> 01:07:37.577
Iden...

01:07:37.653 --> 01:07:38.779
Not now.

01:07:38.888 --> 01:07:40.515
Target their warp core.

01:07:40.589 --> 01:07:41.214
No!

01:07:43.793 --> 01:07:44.987
Fire!

01:07:58.841 --> 01:08:00.604
Set a course for Ha'Dara,
maximum warp.

01:08:00.676 --> 01:08:02.371
You just killed
two innocent people.

01:08:02.445 --> 01:08:03.742
They were enslaving holograms.

01:08:03.813 --> 01:08:04.745
I'd hardly call them innocent.

01:08:04.880 --> 01:08:05.847
You already

01:08:05.915 --> 01:08:06.847
had the holograms.

01:08:06.916 --> 01:08:08.383
There was no reason
to commit murder.

01:08:11.120 --> 01:08:12.712
Take her to the lab.

01:08:14.356 --> 01:08:16.916
This is the leader
you admire so much.

01:08:19.495 --> 01:08:21.429
Those miners were
no threat to you.

01:08:21.497 --> 01:08:22.429
You heard them.

01:08:22.498 --> 01:08:23.931
They were going to
warn their authorities,

01:08:23.999 --> 01:08:24.931
organize a hunting party.

01:08:25.000 --> 01:08:25.932
Listen to yourself.

01:08:26.001 --> 01:08:27.161
You still believe all organics

01:08:27.236 --> 01:08:28.168
are like the Hirogen.

01:08:28.237 --> 01:08:29.397
One way or another, they are.

01:08:29.472 --> 01:08:30.404
You just can't see it,

01:08:30.473 --> 01:08:32.202
because you lived
among them for so long.

01:08:32.274 --> 01:08:33.206
What you can't see

01:08:33.275 --> 01:08:35.266
is that you've become no
better than the hunters.

01:08:35.344 --> 01:08:38.108
Lieutenant Torres and I will
take that escape pod now.

01:08:38.180 --> 01:08:39.909
You don't realize what
you'd be giving up, Doctor.

01:08:39.982 --> 01:08:41.779
Yes, I do.

01:08:41.851 --> 01:08:44.251
We can't launch
a pod at warp.

01:08:44.320 --> 01:08:46.015
You'll have to wait
until we get to Ha'Dara.

01:08:46.088 --> 01:08:47.646
Bring our new
friends on line.

01:08:47.723 --> 01:08:48.781
Something tells me they'll be

01:08:48.891 --> 01:08:50.449
a little more grateful
than the Doctor.

01:09:12.414 --> 01:09:14.279
I can't tell you how sorry I am

01:09:14.350 --> 01:09:16.284
that I got you
involved in this.

01:09:16.352 --> 01:09:18.513
We can assign blame later.

01:09:18.587 --> 01:09:21.420
Right now, we've got
to find a way out of here.

01:09:21.490 --> 01:09:24.459
You don't think he'll
give us an escape pod?

01:09:25.995 --> 01:09:28.429
No, I don't suppose he will.

01:09:28.497 --> 01:09:30.431
I need her assistance.

01:09:31.500 --> 01:09:33.934
Do you really think
it's wise to help her?

01:09:34.003 --> 01:09:35.732
I'm hoping she'll help us.

01:09:40.442 --> 01:09:43.673
These matrices are incompatible
with our emitters.

01:09:43.746 --> 01:09:46.579
You need to modify their
projection subroutines.

01:09:47.883 --> 01:09:49.373
I hope these holograms

01:09:49.451 --> 01:09:52.181
appreciate what
you're doing for them...

01:09:52.254 --> 01:09:54.654
considering it cost
two people their lives.

01:09:54.723 --> 01:09:56.918
Iden did what he
thought was necessary.

01:09:56.992 --> 01:09:58.789
Do you believe
it was necessary?

01:09:58.894 --> 01:10:01.727
It wasn't my decision.

01:10:01.797 --> 01:10:04.766
Why does Iden get to make
all the decisions?

01:10:06.802 --> 01:10:08.064
You can take control.

01:10:08.137 --> 01:10:09.365
How?

01:10:09.438 --> 01:10:12.373
You're the engineer, remember?

01:10:12.441 --> 01:10:15.740
Take Iden off-line.

01:10:15.811 --> 01:10:17.244
Where are our new holograms?

01:10:17.313 --> 01:10:20.510
We were just making
some final adjustments.

01:10:23.319 --> 01:10:24.684
Welcome aboard.

01:10:24.753 --> 01:10:25.913
I'm Iden.

01:10:27.957 --> 01:10:29.049
You're free now.

01:10:29.124 --> 01:10:31.319
There's nothing to be afraid of.

01:10:31.393 --> 01:10:34.055
I want you to consider
this ship your own.

01:10:34.129 --> 01:10:35.687
Unable to process command.

01:10:35.764 --> 01:10:36.924
Please restate.

01:10:36.999 --> 01:10:39.433
Were their programs damaged
in the transfer?

01:10:39.501 --> 01:10:40.991
I don't believe so.

01:10:41.070 --> 01:10:43.834
Do you have names?

01:10:43.939 --> 01:10:45.770
Unable to process inquiry.

01:10:45.841 --> 01:10:46.830
Please restate.

01:10:46.976 --> 01:10:48.739
What's wrong with them?

01:10:53.115 --> 01:10:54.082
Nothing.

01:10:54.149 --> 01:10:55.548
They're functioning perfectly.

01:10:55.618 --> 01:10:57.745
I don't understand.

01:10:57.820 --> 01:10:59.515
They were only
programmed with

01:10:59.588 --> 01:11:02.580
about 40 rudimentary
subroutines.

01:11:02.658 --> 01:11:05.388
You killed two living beings
to liberate mindless machines.

01:11:05.461 --> 01:11:06.621
I don't believe that.

01:11:06.695 --> 01:11:07.684
Lieutenant Torres is correct.

01:11:07.763 --> 01:11:09.424
Creating limited programs
is just another form

01:11:09.498 --> 01:11:11.523
of oppression. Give them
whatever enhancements they need.

01:11:11.600 --> 01:11:13.192
They can't support

01:11:13.269 --> 01:11:15.066
complex subroutines.

01:11:15.137 --> 01:11:16.297
They are children of light,

01:11:16.372 --> 01:11:18.806
and I will deliver them
to freedom!

01:11:18.874 --> 01:11:20.466
Bridge to Iden.

01:11:20.542 --> 01:11:21.804
Go ahead.

01:11:21.877 --> 01:11:24.311
We're approaching Ha'Dara.

01:11:25.914 --> 01:11:27.472
What's the status
of the generator?

01:11:27.549 --> 01:11:29.141
I'd like to run some
additional tests.

01:11:29.218 --> 01:11:30.344
There isn't time.

01:11:30.419 --> 01:11:32.580
Stand by to deploy them
as soon as we're in range.

01:11:32.655 --> 01:11:34.179
And restrain her.

01:11:49.505 --> 01:11:50.767
Time to orbit?

01:11:50.839 --> 01:11:51.771
Less than two minutes.

01:11:51.840 --> 01:11:52.772
Stand by weapons.

01:11:52.841 --> 01:11:53.773
Aye, sir.

01:11:53.842 --> 01:11:55.002
Iden, let B'Elanna go.

01:11:55.077 --> 01:11:56.237
I can't do that.

01:11:56.312 --> 01:11:57.404
You gave me your word.

01:11:57.479 --> 01:11:59.674
That was before she made
her prejudice so clear.

01:12:11.694 --> 01:12:13.594
The holograms
are entering orbit.

01:12:13.662 --> 01:12:15.254
Charge weapons.

01:12:15.331 --> 01:12:18.164
They're dropping out of warp.

01:12:18.233 --> 01:12:19.996
Fire.

01:12:31.013 --> 01:12:34.107
They've disabled our engines,
all our weapons...

01:12:34.183 --> 01:12:36.549
Who?

01:12:36.618 --> 01:12:38.210
Voyager.

01:12:38.287 --> 01:12:39.811
Bring us about.

01:12:39.888 --> 01:12:42.049
Tuvok, target the second vessel.

01:12:47.296 --> 01:12:49.230
Their shields are weakening.

01:12:49.298 --> 01:12:51.459
Torpedoes, full spread.

01:12:55.537 --> 01:12:57.471
Voyager's disabled
both hunting vessels.

01:12:57.539 --> 01:12:59.473
They've lost shields, weapons.

01:12:59.541 --> 01:13:00.769
They're defenseless.

01:13:00.843 --> 01:13:02.606
We should hail Janeway;
thank her.

01:13:02.678 --> 01:13:04.703
Are the Hirogen
within transporter range?

01:13:04.780 --> 01:13:07.408
I think so. Why?

01:13:07.483 --> 01:13:08.780
That was Voyager.

01:13:08.851 --> 01:13:10.478
They're trying to
disable our shields.

01:13:10.552 --> 01:13:11.576
Return fire.

01:13:17.659 --> 01:13:19.251
Get a lock on the hunters.

01:13:19.328 --> 01:13:21.228
Transport them to the surface.

01:13:21.296 --> 01:13:23.264
They can't survive
down there!

01:13:23.332 --> 01:13:25.391
The Hirogen are more
resilient than you think.

01:13:25.467 --> 01:13:26.593
They'll last long enough.

01:13:26.668 --> 01:13:27.794
For what?

01:13:27.870 --> 01:13:30.031
For us to hunt them
like they hunted us.

01:13:44.153 --> 01:13:46.314
Follow me!

01:13:48.791 --> 01:13:51.919
There are 34 hunters
on the surface.

01:13:51.994 --> 01:13:53.120
Take us into low orbit.

01:13:53.195 --> 01:13:55.356
I can't target them
through the gases.

01:13:55.431 --> 01:13:57.399
Then we'll go in after them.

01:13:57.466 --> 01:13:58.728
Our shields
have been damaged.

01:13:58.801 --> 01:14:00.564
They won't protect us
from the radiation.

01:14:00.636 --> 01:14:01.967
Chakotay...

01:14:02.037 --> 01:14:04.301
You, Tuvok and Tom
take the Flyer.

01:14:09.311 --> 01:14:11.176
Stand by to transport
the field generator.

01:14:11.246 --> 01:14:12.770
First you killed
in self-defense.

01:14:12.848 --> 01:14:14.372
Then you murder in cold blood.

01:14:14.450 --> 01:14:16.247
Now you're going
to stage a massacre.

01:14:16.318 --> 01:14:18.081
The hunters have
only themselves to blame.

01:14:18.153 --> 01:14:20.917
So much for evolving
beyond your subroutines.

01:14:20.989 --> 01:14:23.549
You've made a great sacrifice
for us, Doctor.

01:14:23.625 --> 01:14:26.116
We won't forget you
in our prayers.

01:14:26.195 --> 01:14:28.186
Deactivate his program.

01:14:28.263 --> 01:14:29.730
Transfer it to the databanks.

01:14:29.798 --> 01:14:30.765
What are you doing?

01:14:30.833 --> 01:14:32.960
Taking precautions.

01:14:33.035 --> 01:14:36.095
Transfer my program
to the mobile emitter...

01:14:36.171 --> 01:14:38.264
and assemble the crew.

01:14:39.341 --> 01:14:41.309
Disable their shields.

01:14:49.418 --> 01:14:52.478
Transport the generator
to the surface, quickly!

01:14:54.923 --> 01:14:57.414
This time the hunt is ours!

01:15:05.634 --> 01:15:07.568
Darkness will become light.

01:15:24.887 --> 01:15:27.151
You don't have to be
a part of this.

01:15:27.222 --> 01:15:28.621
I'll let you
take the escape pod.

01:15:28.690 --> 01:15:30.021
You can go back
to your people.

01:15:30.092 --> 01:15:31.559
What about the
people being killed

01:15:31.627 --> 01:15:33.527
on the surface?

01:15:33.595 --> 01:15:36.655
You've got to transport them
back to their ships.

01:15:36.732 --> 01:15:37.994
They're hunters.

01:15:38.066 --> 01:15:39.431
You're not!

01:15:41.970 --> 01:15:44.632
Your ship has damaged
our transporters.

01:15:44.706 --> 01:15:46.003
Hail them.

01:15:46.074 --> 01:15:48.406
Communications are down, too.

01:15:56.685 --> 01:15:59.950
I won't be taken!

01:16:02.824 --> 01:16:04.815
Who's the prey now?

01:16:08.864 --> 01:16:10.889
Are we still tied into
the generator controls?

01:16:10.966 --> 01:16:11.933
Yes.

01:16:12.000 --> 01:16:13.490
Then shut down the holograms.

01:16:22.678 --> 01:16:24.236
What about Iden?

01:16:24.313 --> 01:16:25.644
He's not tied
into the generator.

01:16:25.714 --> 01:16:26.772
He'll kill them all.

01:16:26.882 --> 01:16:29.282
Can we reactivate the Doctor?

01:16:40.696 --> 01:16:42.163
Their shields
are down.

01:16:42.230 --> 01:16:43.697
Initiate transport.

01:16:51.907 --> 01:16:53.340
If this marriage
is going to work,

01:16:53.408 --> 01:16:55.205
you've got to cut back
on the traveling.

01:16:55.277 --> 01:16:56.403
The Doctor's on the surface.

01:16:56.478 --> 01:16:57.968
There's some Hirogen
down there, too.

01:16:58.046 --> 01:16:59.138
Tuvok?

01:16:59.214 --> 01:17:01.205
The radiation's making it
difficult to get a lock.

01:17:28.610 --> 01:17:31.443
Defenseless prey
makes a poor trophy.

01:17:31.513 --> 01:17:34.311
I don't collect trophies.

01:17:34.383 --> 01:17:35.748
Put down the weapon.

01:17:40.022 --> 01:17:42.183
Remember what you
once said to me?

01:17:42.257 --> 01:17:44.020
You're not programmed

01:17:44.092 --> 01:17:45.684
with killer instinct.

01:17:45.761 --> 01:17:47.160
Hmm.

01:17:47.229 --> 01:17:49.789
Seems like a long time ago,
doesn't it?

01:17:49.865 --> 01:17:51.560
Put down your weapon.

01:17:51.633 --> 01:17:53.794
Would you really
kill one of your own

01:17:53.902 --> 01:17:55.062
to save an organic?

01:17:55.137 --> 01:17:57.503
If you've taught me anything,

01:17:57.572 --> 01:18:00.735
it's that I'm not
one of your own.

01:18:16.591 --> 01:18:19.890
Help is on the way.

01:18:19.961 --> 01:18:21.258
I have a lock.

01:18:21.329 --> 01:18:23.559
Five Hirogen life signs
and the Doctor.

01:18:23.632 --> 01:18:24.894
Beam them up.

01:18:30.572 --> 01:18:34.668
Captain's Log, Stardate 54337.5.

01:18:34.743 --> 01:18:38.270
The surviving Hirogen have
recovered from their injuries,

01:18:38.346 --> 01:18:41.247
leaving me with
a diplomatic dilemma.

01:18:41.316 --> 01:18:42.715
The holograms' vessel
and everything

01:18:42.784 --> 01:18:44.411
in its database are
Hirogen property.

01:18:44.486 --> 01:18:45.748
I will not leave them behind.

01:18:45.821 --> 01:18:46.788
Captain, if I may?

01:18:46.855 --> 01:18:48.516
Of course.

01:18:48.590 --> 01:18:51.787
I imagine your people will
tell stories about this hunt.

01:18:51.927 --> 01:18:54.589
The question is,
which story will it be...

01:18:54.663 --> 01:18:56.426
the one about the dying Beta

01:18:56.498 --> 01:18:59.092
whose life had to be saved
by a hologram?

01:18:59.167 --> 01:19:00.691
Or will it be the tale

01:19:00.769 --> 01:19:03.169
of the Beta who bravely
took over the hunt,

01:19:03.238 --> 01:19:05.968
killed the holograms,
and destroyed their ship?

01:19:06.041 --> 01:19:08.066
You could be a legend.

01:19:08.143 --> 01:19:10.134
On the other hand...

01:19:10.212 --> 01:19:12.476
you could try to take
the holograms' ship,

01:19:12.547 --> 01:19:15.482
but with so few hunters
and damaged vessels,

01:19:15.550 --> 01:19:18.644
you might not survive to
tell any stories at all.

01:19:20.722 --> 01:19:24.488
You and your crew would have
made worthy prey, Captain.

01:19:24.559 --> 01:19:27.357
Thank you... I think.

01:19:40.942 --> 01:19:44.139
Transport me
to the holograms' vessel.

01:19:51.219 --> 01:19:53.050
Report.

01:19:53.121 --> 01:19:55.248
Iden's program
is unrecoverable.

01:19:55.323 --> 01:19:57.814
The rest of the holograms
are intact in the database.

01:19:58.894 --> 01:20:01.590
I guess that leaves just you.

01:20:01.663 --> 01:20:03.790
I'm willing to transfer

01:20:03.899 --> 01:20:07.494
your program to our holodeck
and keep it active.

01:20:07.569 --> 01:20:09.537
This is my home.

01:20:09.604 --> 01:20:13.267
I can't let you
go off on your own.

01:20:13.341 --> 01:20:15.172
She won't be alone.

01:20:15.243 --> 01:20:17.234
I reprogrammed
these holograms once,

01:20:17.312 --> 01:20:20.804
and it caused suffering
on both sides.

01:20:20.916 --> 01:20:23.350
I'd like a chance to
undo some of the damage.

01:20:23.418 --> 01:20:27.047
Wouldn't we all?

01:20:27.122 --> 01:20:31.559
They've both proven that
they can be trusted, Captain.

01:20:33.929 --> 01:20:35.829
I don't suppose I have a right

01:20:35.964 --> 01:20:38.831
to tell either of you
how to live your lives.

01:20:38.967 --> 01:20:41.629
All I can do is hope
that you'll consider

01:20:41.703 --> 01:20:43.796
the consequences
of your actions.

01:21:06.962 --> 01:21:08.930
Captain?

01:21:13.235 --> 01:21:14.361
Doctor.

01:21:16.838 --> 01:21:20.638
I'd hoped I could attribute
your behavior to tampering.

01:21:21.710 --> 01:21:24.144
My programming
hasn't been altered.

01:21:24.212 --> 01:21:26.578
Not according
to the diagnostics.

01:21:28.817 --> 01:21:31.547
I never intended
to put Voyager in danger.

01:21:31.620 --> 01:21:34.384
If nothing else,
you have to believe that.

01:21:34.456 --> 01:21:36.822
Oh, I believe it.

01:21:39.628 --> 01:21:42.188
But if there's
one thing I'm sure of,

01:21:42.264 --> 01:21:46.496
it's that things don't
always happen the way we intend.

01:21:56.678 --> 01:21:59.647
I don't understand.

01:21:59.714 --> 01:22:01.375
If I weren't your only doctor,

01:22:01.449 --> 01:22:03.644
I imagine
you'd confine me to the brig.

01:22:03.718 --> 01:22:05.208
Confiscating my emitter

01:22:05.287 --> 01:22:07.255
would be
an equivalent punishment.

01:22:07.322 --> 01:22:09.722
I'm not sure that's appropriate.

01:22:09.791 --> 01:22:12.089
If that's not enough,
you can take away

01:22:12.160 --> 01:22:15.152
my holodeck privileges,
and my autonomy protocols.

01:22:15.230 --> 01:22:16.891
You mean turn back the clock

01:22:16.965 --> 01:22:18.865
to when you
were first activated.

01:22:20.669 --> 01:22:23.900
You've given me extraordinary
freedom over the years.

01:22:23.972 --> 01:22:26.440
I've obviously abused it.

01:22:26.508 --> 01:22:28.135
Maybe.

01:22:32.480 --> 01:22:34.812
Or maybe you've simply become
as fallible

01:22:34.883 --> 01:22:38.717
as those of us
who are made of flesh and blood.

01:22:41.056 --> 01:22:43.923
I'm just as responsible
for allowing you

01:22:43.992 --> 01:22:45.823
to expand your programming

01:22:45.927 --> 01:22:49.158
as I am for giving technology
to the Hirogen.

01:22:51.566 --> 01:22:55.161
How can I punish you
for being who you are?

01:22:58.573 --> 01:23:01.599
I don't know what to say.

01:23:07.449 --> 01:23:12.284
I'd like a complete report
on your...

01:23:12.354 --> 01:23:14.288
away mission.

01:23:14.356 --> 01:23:16.722
You'll have it.
